{"actor":{"id":"claude-fable-5","type":"agent"},"content":{"agent":"general-purpose","blocks":[{"text":"# Map: how conversation events are tied to git commits in cledger\n\n## 1. Event schema (`src/schema.ts`)\n\n`EvidenceEvent` fields (src/schema.ts:73-107): `id`, `schema`, `kind`, `occurred_at`, `recorded_at`, `actor {type, id?, display?}`, `producer {tool, version?, source?, session_id?}`, `media_type?`, `content`, `context?`, `conversation? {id, seq}`, `links?`, `raw? {format, data}`, `redactions?`.\n\n**Commit SHA field:** Yes, but only as *informational context*, never as the binding. `RepoContext` (src/schema.ts:47-57) carries:\n\n```ts\n/** HEAD commit SHA at capture time. */\nhead?: string;\n```\n\nplus `repo`, `branch`, `cwd`, `dirty_fingerprint`. It is explicitly *not* part of identity — src/schema.ts:88: `/** Repository context at capture time. Not part of identity. */`.\n\n**Event id** (`eventId`, src/schema.ts:120-134): `\"ev1-\" + sha256Hex(canonicalJson(identity))` where the identity subset is `{schema, kind, occurred_at, actor.{type,id}, source, session_id, conversation, media_type, content, links}`. The doc comment (src/schema.ts:113-119) says why: volatile provenance — `recorded_at`, **`context`** (so the commit SHA), `raw`, `producer.version/tool` — is \"deliberately excluded: a re-ingestion under a different HEAD or adapter version must dedup, not duplicate.\" So the id is a pure content hash of source-determined material, **not** including any commit SHA. Canonical JSON (sorted keys, no whitespace) is in src/canonical.ts:9-24.\n\nThe actual commit binding is therefore **positional** (which note the event line lives in), not schematic.\n\n## 2. Where notes attach (`src/store.ts`, `src/transport.ts`, `src/git.ts`)\n\nPlain `git notes --ref=conversation-ledger` on **ordinary commit objects** — no synthetic anchor object anywhere.\n\n- Ref constants: src/transport.ts:12-13 — `NOTES_NAME = \"conversation-ledger\"`, `NOTES_REF = \"refs/notes/conversation-ledger\"`. Also a staging ref `refs/notes/cledger-incoming` (src/transport.ts:22-23) used only as a fetch landing zone.\n- Storage-model comment, src/store.ts:40-51: \"one git note per **anchor commit** under refs/notes/conversation-ledger. The note body is JSONL — one canonical-JSON event per line, lexicographically sorted, unique... Events are anchored to **HEAD at capture time**, so conversations ride the commit DAG.\"\n- The write, src/store.ts:178-197: `const anchor = await headSha(repo);` then\n\n```ts\nawait git([\"notes\", \"--ref\", NOTES_NAME, \"add\", \"-f\", \"-F\", \"-\", anchor], {...});\n```\n\n  `headSha` is `git rev-parse --verify --quiet HEAD` (src/git.ts:64-70). The note target object is literally the current HEAD commit.\n- Multiple events per commit are handled by read-modify-write of the note body: existing lines read, deduped by id, unioned, **sorted**, rewritten (src/store.ts:183-197). Sorted-unique lines make git's `cat_sort_uniq` notes merge strategy conflict-free (configured per-repo at src/transport.ts:28-37, `notes.conversation-ledger.mergeStrategy = cat_sort_uniq`).\n- Unborn-HEAD special case: if `headSha` is null, events queue in `.git/conversation-ledger/pending.jsonl` (src/store.ts:179-181, 207-217) and are drained into the first real anchor commit (`drainPending`, src/store.ts:220-226; anchor is `null` in the `AppendResult`).\n\n## 3. Capture flow (adapters → `appendEvents`)\n\n- `cledger install` wires **Stop + SessionEnd** hooks into `~/.claude/settings.json` for Claude Code (src/install.ts:52-60) and `[[hooks.Stop]]` into `~/.codex/config.toml` for Codex (src/install.ts:83-93). The hook runs `cledger hook <source>` with the hook payload on stdin (src/cli.ts:366-376).\n- Claude Code adapter (`src/adapters/claude-code.ts`): `runClaudeCodeHook` (line 224) → `captureClaudeTranscript` (line 239) reads the session transcript JSONL, keeps a per-session line cursor at `.git/conversation-ledger/cursors/<session>.json` (lines 79-97) so only new lines are converted, builds `EventDraft`s (`convertLine`, lines 169-197, `conversation.seq` = transcript line index), and calls `appendEvents(repo, drafts)` (line 288). Codex adapter is identical in structure (`appendEvents` at src/adapters/codex.ts:366).\n- **Which commit?** `appendEvents` resolves the anchor itself: `context` = `captureContext` (repo/branch/HEAD/dirty fingerprint, src/store.ts:66-78) stamped on each draft, then inside the lock `anchor = await headSha(repo)` (src/store.ts:178). So every turn attaches to **whatever HEAD is at the moment the Stop/SessionEnd hook fires** — typically the pre-existing commit the conversation is producing work *on top of*, dirty tree noted only via `context.dirty_fingerprint` (sha256 of `git status --porcelain`, src/store.ts:76).\n- **Handling for the anchor commit later disappearing (rebase/squash/amend): none.** There is no post-rewrite hook, no `git replace`, no remapping, no re-anchor code anywhere in src/. The only mitigations are indirect:\n  - Notes on unreachable commits are still enumerable and are still read by default (see Q4) — data isn't lost, it just falls out of branch-scoped views.\n  - Event ids exclude HEAD, so a hypothetical recapture under a new commit dedups instead of duplicating (src/schema.ts:113-119).\n  - The problem is explicitly acknowledged as a known limitation + roadmap item (`re-anchor`), see Q5.\n\n## 4. Read/query flow (`cledger log` / `show` / `conversations` / `export` / `scan`)\n\nIt **lists all notes**, then optionally filters by reachability — it does not walk commits looking up notes per-commit.\n\n- `readEvents` (src/store.ts:242-263): first `absorbIncoming` (fold fetched staging ref in, src/transport.ts:193-223), then `listAnchors` = `git notes --ref conversation-ledger list` parsed to the annotated-object SHAs (src/store.ts:98-108). If `opts.reachableFrom` is set, anchors are intersected with `revList(repo, rev)` = `git rev-list <rev>` (src/git.ts:130-133): `anchors = anchors.filter((a) => reachable.has(a))` (src/store.ts:246-249). Then each surviving anchor's note is read (`git notes show <anchor>`, src/store.ts:80-86), pending.jsonl appended, kind/source/conversation filters applied, and results sorted by conversation → seq → time → id (`sortEvents`, src/store.ts:266-276).\n- CLI defaults (src/cli.ts:108-115): `cledger log` defaults `reachableFrom = \"HEAD\"`; `--rev R` scopes to R; `--all` drops the reachability filter entirely. `show` and `conversations`/`export` use `readEvents` too (`show` passes no reachability filter — conversation-prefix only, src/cli.ts:182).\n- **Orphaned anchor behavior:** `git notes list` enumerates notes regardless of whether the target commit is reachable, and `git notes show <sha>` works as long as the commit object physically exists. So after a rebase/squash: `cledger log` (HEAD-scoped) silently *omits* those conversations; `cledger log --all`, `show`, and `export` still see them. If the orphaned commit is eventually GC'd, `readNoteLines` uses `allowFailure: true` (src/store.ts:81-85) and returns `\"\"` — the events vanish silently, no error. There is no detection or warning for either state. This exact behavior is documented at docs/WIP_TECHNICAL_DESIGN.md:97-102 (\"Known limitation: squash merges ... conversations remain in the ledger (notes are enumerable regardless of reachability; `cledger log --all` sees them) but drop out of the target branch's reachability view. A future `re-anchor` operation is the intended fix.\").\n\n## 5. Exhaustive grep: squash / rebase / rewrite / remap / mapping / orphan / unreachable / amend / cherry-pick\n\n**Zero hits anywhere for:** `rebase`, `remap`, `amend`, `cherry-pick`/`cherry` (across src/, docs/, README, tests). No hits for `git replace` either.\n\nHits about **commit-anchor** rewriting (the ones relevant to your question):\n\n| Location | Content |\n|---|---|\n| docs/WIP_TECHNICAL_DESIGN.md:97-102 | \"**Known limitation: squash merges**\" section — sq