acks off from `core.hooksPath` and non-shell hooks with a once-per-repo warning, transport.ts:71-84) and adds the fetch refspec to `remote.origin.fetch` (transport.ts:164-184). The hook calls `cledger transport-push \"$1\"` (transport.ts:52-68) → `transportPush()` (store.ts:410-437): pushes the ledger alongside the user's push; a `ScanBlockedError` holds back only the ledger by default, or aborts the whole push with `transport.strict: true` (store.ts:423-431, cli.ts:254-258); any other error warns and never fails the user's push.\n\n**Scan gate** (store.ts:289-349): `remoteNoteIds` fetches the remote ref into throwaway `refs/notes/conversation-ledger-scan-tmp`, collects event ids, deletes the temp ref (store.ts:296-307); only events the remote lacks are scanned (store.ts:332) — already-pushed events are never rescanned.\n\n## 2. `redactEvent` — `src/store.ts:510-688`\n\nStep by step:\n1. Validates exactly one of `--pattern` / `--all` (store.ts:515-519).\n2. Under the dir-based lock (store.ts:110-133, 10s steal timeout), `locateEvent` finds the unique event by id prefix across all anchors + pending.jsonl; errors on zero or ambiguous matches (store.ts:455-485).\n3. Rewrite: `--pattern` runs `redactDraft` with a synthetic `manual` rule over content+raw, errors if nothing matched (store.ts:537-562; optionally collects matched values for the opt-in known-secrets store, store.ts:559-562); `--all` replaces content with `[REDACTED:manual:<12-hex fingerprint>]` and drops `raw` entirely (store.ts:563-568).\n4. **CRITICAL id preservation** (comment at store.ts:573-584): the rewritten draft explicitly carries `id: original.id` (store.ts:585-589) and `finalizeEvent` honors a supplied id (`draft.id ?? eventId(draft)`, schema.ts:140). Rationale in the comment: ids are a pure function of source content (schema.ts:120-134), so if the id were recomputed from the redacted content, a later transcript rescan would regenerate the original unredacted event under the *old* id, dedup wouldn