taining a fake secret, and seeds the remote via `sync(repo, \"origin\", \"push\", { skipScan: true })` — skipScan because this secret shape would trip the keyword-assignment scan rule, and pushing the pre-redaction content *is* the test's precondition (161-163). It then monkey-patches `process.stderr.write` to capture output, runs `redactEvent` with `--pattern`, restores stderr, and asserts `result.squashed === false` and that stderr contained \"skipping the local squash\" (179-183).\n\n## 5. Force-push, ref rewriting, notes history, fresh-clone bootstrap\n\n- **No force-push anywhere.** The push is a plain `NOTES_REF:NOTES_REF` (store.ts:385); the fetch refspecs use `+` (force-fetch) but only into the staging/temp refs, never the local ledger ref — \"the local ref is never force-overwritten — absorption is always the cat_sort_uniq union\" (transport.ts:18-20; echoed in README.md:69 and docs/WIP_TECHNICAL_DESIGN.md:127).\n- **Notes commits are chained.** `refs/notes/conversation-ledger` has normal commit history: every `git notes add -f` creates a new notes commit parented on the previous one, and `notes merge` creates merge commits. The redact test asserts this by checking `git log --oneline NOTES_REF` collapses to exactly 1 commit after squash (redact-command.test.ts:73-74). The only ref rewriting in the codebase is that redaction squash — `commit-tree` (parentless) + `update-ref` (store.ts:669-675) — and it's gated on origin not having the ref yet.\n- **Purging already-pushed history is explicitly deferred**: the warning (store.ts:678-684), README.md:146, and docs/WIP_TECHNICAL_DESIGN.md:231, 302 all describe post-push purge (force-push notes ref + collaborator re-fetch coordination) as separate, not-yet-built tooling.\n- **Fresh clone bootstrap**: a plain `git clone` doesn't bring notes refs. Two paths in: (a) explicit `cledger sync` / `cledger sync --fetch`, which fetches into INCOMING_REF and absorbs (and `absorbIncoming` fast-adopts via `update-ref` when ther