{"actor":{"id":"claude-sonnet-5","type":"agent"},"content":{"agent":"general-purpose","blocks":[{"text":"# Conversation-Capture Adapter Reference: Claude Code + Codex CLI\n\n## Part A — Claude Code\n\n### A1. Hook registration (`~/.claude/settings.json`)\n\nYour current file is minimal — no `hooks` key at all, so any install can add one non-destructively:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"model\": \"claude-fable-5[1m]\",\n  \"enabledPlugins\": {\n    \"clangd-lsp@claude-plugins-official\": true,\n    \"codex@openai-codex\": true\n  },\n  \"extraKnownMarketplaces\": {\n    \"openai-codex\": { \"source\": { \"source\": \"github\", \"repo\": \"openai/codex-plugin-cc\" } }\n  },\n  \"theme\": \"dark\",\n  \"preferredNotifChannel\": \"notifications_disabled\"\n}\n```\n(`~/.claude/settings.local.json` only holds a `permissions.allow` list — no hooks there either.) Merge by adding a top-level `\"hooks\"` object; don't touch existing keys.\n\n**Registration shape** (per [code.claude.com/docs/en/hooks](https://code.claude.com/docs/en/hooks)):\n```json\n{\n  \"hooks\": {\n    \"Stop\": [\n      { \"hooks\": [ { \"type\": \"command\", \"command\": \"/path/to/capture.sh\", \"timeout\": 30 } ] }\n    ],\n    \"SessionEnd\": [\n      { \"hooks\": [ { \"type\": \"command\", \"command\": \"/path/to/finalize.sh\", \"timeout\": 60 } ] }\n    ]\n  }\n}\n```\n`matcher` (tool name/regex) is only meaningful for `PreToolUse`/`PostToolUse`-style events; `Stop`/`SessionEnd`/`UserPromptSubmit` ignore it. Hook `type` can be `command` (most common), plus `http`/`mcp_tool`/`prompt`/`agent`. Default timeout 600s for `command`.\n\n**Relevant events**: `SessionStart` (`startup|resume|clear|compact`), `UserPromptSubmit`, `PreToolUse`/`PostToolUse` (matcher = tool name), `Stop` (assistant finishes responding — fires **per completed turn**), `SubagentStop`, `PreCompact`/`PostCompact`, `SessionEnd` (reason: `clear|resume|logout|prompt_input_exit|other`).\n\n**Stdin JSON** — common fields on every hook: `session_id`, `prompt_id`, `transcript_path`, `cwd`, `permission_mode`, `hook_event_name`. `Stop` additionally supplies `last_assistant_message` (use this instead of re-reading the file — `transcript_path` can lag). `SessionEnd` gives `reason` but not `last_assistant_message`.\n\n**Recommendation**: hook **`Stop`** for per-turn capture (fires after each completed assistant turn, gives you `transcript_path` + `last_assistant_message` directly on stdin — no polling needed), and **`SessionEnd`** for a final full-session sync/archive/cleanup pass. Both fire per Claude Code session (one process = one `session_id` = one project subdirectory).\n\n### A2. Transcript format (`~/.claude/projects/<escaped-cwd>/<session-id>.jsonl`)\n\nInspected `~/.claude/projects/-Users-evintunador-dev-ds4-gateway/*.jsonl` and others. Directory name is the cwd with `/` and `.` replaced by `-`; the repo/branch is *not* baked into the directory name, only into each line's `cwd`/`gitBranch` fields. Line `type` values observed: `user`, `assistant`, `system`, `summary`, plus session-bookkeeping types (`ai-title`, `last-prompt`, `mode`, `permission-mode`, `attachment`, `file-history-snapshot`, `file-history-delta`, `queue-operation`).\n\nCommon envelope fields on `user`/`assistant`/`system` lines: `type`, `uuid`, `parentUuid` (linked-list threading; `null` for the first line), `sessionId`, `timestamp` (ISO8601), `cwd`, `gitBranch`, `version` (e.g. `\"2.1.214\"`), `userType` (`\"external\"`), `isSidechain` (bool — `true` for subagent-spawned messages), `entrypoint`. No commit hash field — only branch + cwd identify the repo state.\n\n```jsonc\n// type=user, plain text\n{\"type\":\"user\",\"message\":{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":\"...\"}, \"cwd\":\"...\", \"gitBranch\":\"main\",\n \"sessionId\":\"...\", \"uuid\":\"...\", \"parentUuid\":\"...\", \"timestamp\":\"...\", \"version\":\"2.1.214\", ...}\n\n// type=user, carrying a tool_result (reply to prior tool_use)\n{\"type\":\"user\",\"message\":{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[\n   {\"type\":\"tool_result\",\"tool_use_id\":\"toolu_...\",\"content\":\"...[elided]...\"}]}, ...}\n\n// type=assistant — content blocks: thinking / text / tool_use\n{\"type\":\"assistant\",\"message\":{\"model\":\"claude-fable-5\",\"id\":\"msg_...\",\"role\":\"assistant\",\n   \"content\":[{\"type\":\"thinking\",\"thinking\":\"\",\"signature\":\"...\"}],\n   \"stop_reason\":\"tool_use\",\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":2,\"output_tokens\":72,...}}, ...}\n{\"type\":\"assistant\",\"message\":{\"content\":[\n   {\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"id\":\"toolu_...\",\"name\":\"Read\",\"input\":{\"file_path\":\"...\"}}]}, ...}\n\n// type=system — turn/session bookkeeping, no message content\n{\"type\":\"system\",\"subtype\":\"turn_duration\",\"durationMs\":19583,\"messageCount\":9,\"isMeta\":false, ...}\n{\"type\":\"system\",\"subtype\":\"away_summary\", ...}\n```\n`subtype:\"turn_duration\"` system lines are emitted at the end of each turn inside the transcript itself — a secondary in-band signal that a turn ended, but the `Stop` hook is the reliable external trigger. `summary` lines (compaction summaries) exist as a type but none appeared in the sampled files.\n\n## Part B — Codex CLI\n\nInstalled version: **codex-cli 0.144.6**.\n\n### B1. `~/.codex/config.toml` (current contents)\n```toml\nmodel = \"gpt-5.6-sol\"\nmodel_reasoning_effort = \"medium\"\napprovals_reviewer = \"auto_review\"\n[projects.\"/Users/evintunador\"]\ntrust_level = \"trusted\"\n[projects.\"/Users/evintunador/repos/BandaruDheeraj/sticky-note\"]\ntrust_level = \"trusted\"\n[projects.\"/Users/evintunador/dev/ds4-gateway\"]\ntrust_level = \"trusted\"\n[tui.model_availability_nux]\n\"gpt-5.6-sol\" = 4\n```\nNo `notify` or `[hooks]`/`features.hooks` entries present — clean slate for merging.\n\nTwo mechanisms exist:\n1. **`notify`** (legacy, stable): `notify = [\"/bin/bash\", \"/path/to/notify.sh\"]`. Fires only on `agent-turn-complete`. Payload arrives as a **single JSON string in `argv[1]`** (not stdin): `{\"type\":\"agent-turn-complete\",\"last-assistant-message\":\"...\",\"input-messages\":[...]}`.\n2. **Hooks engine** (new, stable since ~v0.124, April 2026 — matches your 0.144.6 install): declared via `[[hooks.<Event>]]` blocks in `config.toml` or `hooks.json`, mirroring Claude Code's hook shape almost field-for-field:\n```toml\n[[hooks.Stop]]\n[[hooks.Stop.hooks]]\ntype = \"command\"\ncommand = '/path/to/capture.sh'\ntimeout = 30\n```\nEvents: `SessionStart`, `UserPromptSubmit`, `PreToolUse`, `PostToolUse`, `PreCompact`, `PostCompact`, `SubagentStart`, `SubagentStop`, `Stop` (turn-scope). Stdin JSON: `session_id`, `transcript_path`, `cwd`, `hook_event_name`, `model`, `permission_mode`, `turn_id` (turn-scoped events), plus event-specific fields (`tool_name`/`tool_input` for tool events). May need `features.hooks = true` gating in some builds — worth a runtime check (`codex --help` / probing for a hook firing) before relying on it, since docs on this are newer and thinner than Claude Code's.\n\n### B2. Rollout files (`~/.codex/sessions/YYYY/MM/DD/rollout-<ts>-<uuid>.jsonl`, uncompressed here)\n\nLine `type`: `session_meta` (once, first line), `turn_context` (once per turn), `event_msg`, `response_item`, `world_state`.\n\n```jsonc\n{\"type\":\"session_meta\",\"payload\":{\"session_id\":\"019f7624-...\",\"cwd\":\"/Users/evintunador\",\n  \"originator\":\"codex-tui\",\"cli_version\":\"0.144.5\",\"model_provider\":\"openai\",\n  \"base_instructions\":{\"text\":\"...[system prompt, elided]...\"}, \"history_mode\":\"legacy\"}}\n\n{\"type\":\"turn_context\",\"payload\":{\"turn_id\":\"019f7624-...\",\"cwd\":\"...\",\"workspace_roots\":[...],\n  \"approval_policy\":\"on-request\",\"sandbox_policy\":{...},\"model\":\"gpt-5.6-luna\",\"effort\":\"low\"}}\n\n{\"type\":\"event_msg\",\"payload\":{\"type\":\"task_started\",\"turn_id\":\"...\",\"model_context_window\":258400}}\n{\"type\":\"event_msg\",\"payload\":{\"type\":\"user_message\",\"message\":\"...[elided]...\",\"images\":[]}}\n{\"type\":\"event_msg\",\"payload\":{\"type\":\"agent_message\",\"message\":\"...[elided]...\",\"phase\":\"commentary\"}}\n{\"type\":\"event_msg\",\"payload\":{\"type\":\"token_count\",\"rate_limits\":{...}}}\n{\"type\":\"event_msg\",\"payload\":{\"type\":\"turn_aborted\",\"reason\":\"interrupted\",\"duration_ms\":2621}}\n\n// response_item.payload.type: message | reasoning | function_call | function_call_output\n//                              | custom_tool_call | custom_tool_call_output\n{\"type\":\"response_item\",\"payload\":{\"type\":\"message\",\"role\":\"user\",\n  \"content\":[{\"type\":\"input_text\",\"text\":\"<environment_context>...[elided]\"}]}}\n{\"type\":\"response_item\",\"payload\":{\"type\":\"message\",\"role\":\"assistant\",\n  \"content\":[{\"type\":\"output_text\",\"text\":\"...[elided]\"}], \"phase\":\"commentary\"}}\n{\"type\":\"response_item\",\"payload\":{\"type\":\"reasoning\",\"id\":\"rs_...\",\"summary\":[],\n  \"encrypted_content\":\"gAAAAA...[opaque, encrypted]...\"}}\n{\"type\":\"response_item\",\"payload\":{\"type\":\"function_call\",\"name\":\"wait\",\n  \"arguments\":\"{\\\"cell_id\\\":\\\"9\\\",...}\",\"call_id\":\"call_...\"}}\n{\"type\":\"response_item\",\"payload\":{\"type\":\"function_call_output\",\"call_id\":\"call_...\",\n  \"output\":[{\"type\":\"input_text\",\"text\":\"...[elided shell output]...\"}]}}\n{\"type\":\"response_item\",\"payload\":{\"type\":\"custom_tool_call\",\"name\":\"exec\",\n  \"input\":\"const r = await tools.exec_command({...}); text(r.output);\"}}\n```\nNo `gitBranch` field observed; repo/cwd context comes only from `session_meta.payload.cwd` / `turn_context.payload.cwd`. Reasoning content is encrypted and not human-readable — capture must rely on `message`/`event_msg` text, not `reasoning`.\n\n### B3. Recommended capture trigger\n\n**Use the new Codex hooks engine's `Stop` event** (turn-scope, same semantics as Claude Code's `Stop`) rather than `notify` or file-watching — it's the direct an