{"actor":{"id":"claude-sonnet-5","type":"agent"},"content":{"agent":"general-purpose","blocks":[{"text":"## Findings\n\nI reviewed the diff, `src/adapters/codex.ts`, `src/schema.ts`, `src/adapters/drift.ts`, `src/cli.ts`, and inspected 37 real rollout files under `~/.codex/sessions/**` (1503 real reasoning items) with Python, including cross-referencing parent/subagent session pairs.\n\n**1. cledger's own `redact`/`scan` pipeline can irreversibly destroy the exact ciphertext this feature exists to preserve.** `src/redact/scan.ts:99-100` calls `walkStrings(event.raw.data, ...)` unconditionally for every event kind — there is no `kind === \"reasoning\"` exemption anywhere in `scan.ts` or `redact/apply.ts` (grep confirms zero hits). The paranoid-tier `high-entropy` rule (`src/redact/rules.ts`, pattern `\\b[A-Za-z0-9+/_=-]{24,}\\b`, entropy-gated at 4.0 bits/char) will fire on essentially every real `encrypted_content` blob I checked: they're single base64url runs of ~1200-1600+ chars, all within that character class, well above the entropy threshold. Following the documented remedy (`cledger redact <id> --pattern|--all`), `redactDraft` (`apply.ts:144-148`) rewrites matched spans in `raw.data`, and the `--all` path (`store.ts:798-801,826`) deletes `raw` entirely and blanks `content`; `redactEvent` then squashes local notes history when unpushed (`store.ts:897-911`), making the original blob unrecoverable. This directly contradicts the roadmap's own claim that reasoning is \"excluded from...secret scans, which cannot scan ciphertext anyway\" (README diff) — that exclusion was never implemented.\n\n**2. Subagent/guardian rollout files collapse into the parent's `conversation.id` with colliding `seq`.** `codex.ts:326-335` overwrites `sessionId` with `session_meta.payload.session_id` whenever present — but for subagent/guardian threads, that field is the *parent's* id, not the file's own (`session_meta.payload.id`). Verified real collision: `.../rollout-...-019f7650-...c89d-....jsonl` line 8 (`message`) and `.../rollout-...-019f7711-...ce59b5a0515e.jsonl` (a \"guardian\" auto-review subagent, model `codex-auto-review`) line 8 (`reasoning`) both produce `conversation={id:\"codex:019f7650-...\", seq:8}` — unrelated content from unrelated files, same identity tuple. The file's own distinguishing id is never stored anywhere (not in `producer.session_id`, not raw — see #3), so a consumer can't tell these apart or know one came from an internal safety-review thread rather than the user's real conversation.\n\n**3. `session_meta`/`turn_context` — the only lines carrying `model`, `model_provider`, `cli_version`, `thread_source` — are dropped with zero trace.** `KNOWN_SKIPPED_LINE_TYPES` (`codex.ts:53-60`) causes these to fall through `convertLine`'s `line.type !== \"response_item\"` check with no `unrecognizedDraft` fallback (that only applies to *response_item* payload types). `reasoningDraft` (`drift.ts`) carries none of this either. No stored `reasoning` event anywhere records which model/provider/CLI-version produced it — a replay consumer has nothing in the ledger to check compatibility against.\n\n(Not a gap: `conversation.seq` = raw line index correctly preserves intra-file ordering; `internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough.turn_id` and the reasoning `id` are preserved losslessly since `raw.data` is the unmodified line; `export` always includes `raw` for every kind, no silent omission there.)","type":"text"}],"role":"assistant"},"context":{"branch":"main","cwd":"/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/conversation-ledger","head":"de79e501289e2e19946780867779ef465ead2124","repo":"git@github.com:evintunador/conversation-ledger.git"},"conversation":{"id":"claude-code:ca50d7db-8621-495c-a94a-c3d3ab731073#agent:af4142a7fa06faa87","parent":"claude-code:ca50d7db-8621-495c-a94a-c3d3ab731073","seq":85},"id":"ev1-ea43824208379972653a3e2696eae25864f96c537b1a4ab9e510a0b7a84a0b4e","kind":"conversation_turn","occurred_at":"2026-07-22T21:26:38.537Z",