e\n54:                                            current branch; --all pushes the whole ledger,\n55:                                            --rev scopes to another branch/commit\n56:   cledger transport-push [remote]         pre-push hook entrypoint (installed automatically):\n57:                                            pushes the ledger ref alongside git push, scoped to the\n58:                                            refs being pushed (read from git's pre-push stdin;\n59:                                            falls back to HEAD); scan findings hold back only the\n60:                                            ledger unless transport.strict\n61:   cledger scan [--all|--rev R] [--paranoid]   scan local events for potential secrets (CI-friendly:\n62:                                            exits 1 if any finding, 0 otherwise); default scope is\n63:                                            every local event, --rev restricts by reachability\n64:   cledger inspect <event-id-prefix> [--context N] [--reveal] [--stdout] [--force]\n65:                                            show a finding with real surrounding context (default 400\n66:                                            chars each side). Writes to a file outside the repo and\n67:                                            refuses to run inside a coding-agent session — reports\n68:                                            never print content, because reprinting it re-seeds the\n69:                                            finding. HUMANS ONLY, in a plain terminal.\n70:   cledger allow <fingerprint...>          mark scan finding fingerprint(s) as known false positives\n71:   cledger redact <event-id-prefix> (--pattern REGEX | --all) [--reason TEXT]\n72:                                            rewrite an existing event to remove a secret, keeping its\n73:                                            id stable, and squash local notes history if unpushed\n74:   cledger re-anchor [--apply] [-