{"actor":{"id":"deepseek-v4-flash","type":"agent"},"content":{"agent":"explore","blocks":[{"id":"call_fadfb20b4cededde9f9b9bf84aa1c2ad","input":{"filePath":"/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/conversation-ledger/docs/PRODUCT_INTENT.md"},"name":"read","type":"tool_use"},{"content":"<path>/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/conversation-ledger/docs/PRODUCT_INTENT.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: # Product intent\n2: \n3: ## Purpose\n4: \n5: Conversation Ledger preserves durable, inspectable records of visible\n6: conversations between people and coding agents. It is a general conversation\n7: provenance primitive, not an intent-analysis product. Downstream consumers may\n8: use its records as evidence about why a repository changed, but the ledger must\n9: not impose that interpretation.\n10: \n11: The record must remain useful to consumers beyond a single tool: cross-CLI\n12: continuity, archival/export, code attribution, review, and later intent\n13: retrieval are all valid independent uses.\n14: \n15: ## Behavioral commitments\n16: \n17: - Preserve source material and provenance; do not silently rewrite history.\n18: - Preserve exact visible turns before creating optional derived views.\n19: - Retain enough provenance for consumers to determine applicability without\n20:   treating any record as timeless truth.\n21: - Record the repository, branch, commit, worktree state, author, timestamps,\n22:   and capture mechanism with each artifact whenever available.\n23: - Keep storage out of ordinary working-tree status views while retaining normal\n24:   Git durability and shareability.\n25: - Make sharing, retention, redaction, and deletion deliberate user choices.\n26: \n27: ## Non-goals for the foundation\n28: \n29: - Deciding which historical statement is correct or intended.\n30: - Summarizing, ranking, embedding, or otherwise interpreting conversations.\n31: - Controlling an agent, enforcing a workflow, or orchestrating agents.\n32: - Decrypting, inte