{"actor":{"type":"system"},"content":{"blocks":[{"content":"# AgentLogs: AI Coding Agent Transcript Management\n\n## What It Does\n\nAgentLogs is an open-source platform that \"captures and analyzes transcripts from AI coding agents\" including Claude Code, Cline, Codex, OpenCode, and Pi. It provides team visibility into how these tools are used within codebases.\n\n## Core Features\n\n**Team Observability**: The platform offers dashboards showing activity metrics, agent and model usage, plus per-member breakdowns.\n\n**Git Integration**: AgentLogs \"links sessions to the commits they produced,\" enabling teams to see which transcript generated which code changes.\n\n**Shared Learning**: Teams can browse and share sessions to discover effective prompts and workflows.\n\n## Data Storage Architecture\n\nAgentLogs stores data **server-side**, not in git references. The system uses:\n- SQLite databases for structured data\n- Local blob storage on disk for transcripts\n- Self-hosted deployment options via Docker containers or standalone binaries\n\nData can be hosted on AgentLogs Cloud or self-hosted on your own infrastructure.\n\n## Redaction & Provenance\n\nWhile the documentation mentions \"secret redaction\" capabilities in the shared packages, specific implementation details aren't detailed in this content. The system does track commit associations and transcript metadata for provenance purposes.\n\n## Licensing\n\nAgentLogs uses FSL-1.1-Apache-2.0 license, making it source-available for self-hosting.","tool_use_id":"toolu_01BzB2Mt5rrkuHW4rbiqsPMn","type":"tool_result"}],"role":"user"},"context":{"branch":"main","cwd":"/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/conversation-ledger","head":"de79e501289e2e19946780867779ef465ead2124","repo":"git@github.com:evintunador/conversation-ledger.git"},"conversation":{"id":"claude-code:700cd82f-2f79-4cd6-b727-0f81230e0837#agent:af424cc63295b8016","parent":"claude-code:700cd82f-2f79-4cd6-b727-0f81230e0837","seq":41},"id":"ev1-a7f6aed0