{"actor":{"type":"system"},"content":{"blocks":[{"content":"# Hook Trust and Persistence Mechanism\n\nYes, hooks require review and trust before they can run. Here's how the system works:\n\n## Trust Review Process\n\nNon-managed command hooks must be reviewed and explicitly trusted by users before execution. Codex displays configured hooks and requires approval for each one. The system records trust against the hook's current hash, so any modifications trigger a re-review requirement.\n\nAs stated in the documentation: *\"Before a non-managed command hook can run, Codex requires you to review and trust the exact hook definition.\"*\n\n## Persistence\n\nTrust decisions are persisted locally. Users can manage hook trust through the `/hooks` command in the CLI, where they can inspect hook sources, review new or changed hooks, enable/disable individual hooks, and confirm trust decisions.\n\n## Managed Hooks Exception\n\nHooks from enterprise, system, MDM, cloud, or `requirements.toml` sources are marked as \"managed\" and automatically trusted by policy—they bypass the user review requirement since administrators control them.\n\n## Bypassing Trust (Temporary)\n\nFor one-off automation, the `--dangerously-bypass-hook-trust` flag allows hooks to run without persisted trust reviews for that single invocation, though this is intended only for pre-vetted scenarios.","tool_use_id":"toolu_01WdsYv1YxpCwvo4sMFoKenD","type":"tool_result"}],"role":"user"},"context":{"branch":"main","cwd":"/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/conversation-ledger","head":"de79e501289e2e19946780867779ef465ead2124","repo":"git@github.com:evintunador/conversation-ledger.git"},"conversation":{"id":"claude-code:700cd82f-2f79-4cd6-b727-0f81230e0837#agent:a64e77f6bcddcbe2b","parent":"claude-code:700cd82f-2f79-4cd6-b727-0f81230e0837","seq":15},"id":"ev1-b54abacc9943e485652776e2234b29522f136f45a165938c8b37a68c1f08916a","kind":"conversation_turn","occurred_at":"2026-07-18T22:51:47.674Z","producer":{"session