{"actor":{"type":"system"},"content":{"blocks":[{"content":"# `features.hooks` Configuration\n\n## What is it?\n\n`features.hooks` is a configuration option that enables lifecycle hooks in Codex. According to the reference, it allows you to \"Enable lifecycle hooks loaded from `hooks.json` or inline `[hooks]`\" configuration.\n\n## Is it Required?\n\nNo, it is not required. The documentation indicates this feature is `off by default`, meaning you only need to enable it if you want to use hooks functionality.\n\n## Available Configuration Options\n\nThe reference documents several hook-related configuration settings:\n\n1. **`features.hooks`** (boolean) — Enables the hooks feature itself\n2. **`hooks`** (table) — Allows you to define lifecycle hooks directly in your `config.toml` file\n3. **`hooks.<Event>`** — Matcher groups for specific events like `PreToolUse`, `PostToolUse`, `SessionStart`, `Stop`, and others\n4. **`hooks.<Event>[].hooks`** — Handlers for matched events (currently supporting command hooks)\n5. **`hooks.<Event>[].hooks[].commandWindows`** — Windows-specific command overrides\n\nThe documentation notes that hooks use \"the same event schema as `hooks.json`\" and directs you to the Hooks guide for comprehensive examples and supported event types.","tool_use_id":"toolu_01AKXLVN1GuQ3N5FecKDrG1G","type":"tool_result"}],"role":"user"},"context":{"branch":"main","cwd":"/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/conversation-ledger","head":"de79e501289e2e19946780867779ef465ead2124","repo":"git@github.com:evintunador/conversation-ledger.git"},"conversation":{"id":"claude-code:700cd82f-2f79-4cd6-b727-0f81230e0837#agent:a64e77f6bcddcbe2b","parent":"claude-code:700cd82f-2f79-4cd6-b727-0f81230e0837","seq":20},"id":"ev1-ee41ecedccefe4f3a0833ea9f6a45ded34959a9492e18480426e76e0bf61bc38","kind":"conversation_turn","occurred_at":"2026-07-18T22:51:56.693Z","producer":{"session_id":"700cd82f-2f79-4cd6-b727-0f81230e0837","source":"claude-code","source_version":"2.1.214","too