mestamps,\n  and capture mechanism with each artifact whenever available.\n- Keep storage out of ordinary working-tree status views while retaining normal\n  Git durability and shareability.\n- Make sharing, retention, redaction, and deletion deliberate user choices.\n\n## Non-goals for the foundation\n\n- Deciding which historical statement is correct or intended.\n- Summarizing, ranking, embedding, or otherwise interpreting conversations.\n- Controlling an agent, enforcing a workflow, or orchestrating agents.\n- Capturing reasoning the provider hides (visible reasoning is recorded when\n  exposed), or claiming it can reproduce a native agent session.\n\nThose belong to clients such as Turnbridge and Intent Recall, not to this core\nstorage layer.\n","filePath":"/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/conversation-ledger/docs/PRODUCT_INTENT.md","numLines":37,"startLine":1,"totalLines":37},"type":"text"},"type":"user","userType":"external","uuid":"3f4750eb-9b91-42f5-aac4-faa3ba8a38ba","version":"2.1.216"},"format":"claude-code-jsonl/1"},"recorded_at":"2026-08-11T11:07:24.924Z","schema":"conversation-ledger/v1"}
{"actor":{"type":"system"},"content":{"blocks":[{"content":"1\t# Product intent\n2\t\n3\t## Purpose\n4\t\n5\tIntent Recall helps later humans and coding agents find evidence of intended\n6\tbehavior when code, tests, and documentation are incomplete, ambiguous, or in\n7\tconflict. It is built on the premise that each implementation artifact is a\n8\tlossy expression of a human goal, and that independently preserved sources can\n9\treduce correlated misunderstanding.\n10\t\n11\t## Behavioral commitments\n12\t\n13\t- Return evidence with citations, chronology, and provenance—not unsupported\n14\t  claims about intent.\n15\t- Distinguish an original request, implementation decision, later correction,\n16\t  and unresolved disagreement.\n17\t- Prefer explicit human statements over an inference from the present code.\n18\t- Make uncertainty and contradictory evidence visible.\n19\t- Preserve the ability to inspect the raw record behind any structured view.\n20\t- Avoid turning historical material into a mechanism for silently overruling a\n21\t  current human instruction.\n22\t\n23\t## Non-goals\n24\t\n25\t- Establishing a single permanent truth for a repository.\n26\t- Replacing product judgment or user confirmation.\n27\t- Capturing sessions or transferring conversations between tools.\n28\t\n29\t## Relationship to Conversation Ledger and Turnbridge\n30\t\n31\tIntent Recall reads Conversation Ledger directly. Turnbridge is one valuable producer\n32\tof conversational evidence, but Lens must also support decisions and artifacts\n33\tthat arrived through other ingestion paths.\n34\t","tool_use_id":"toolu_016Njq3uVL64gUrodVqCFmK6","type":"tool_result"}],"role":"user"},"context":{"branch":"main","cwd":"/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/conversation-ledger","head":"de79e501289e2e19946780867779ef465ead2124","repo":"git@github.com:evintunador/conversation-ledger.git"},"conversation":{"id":"claude-code:700cd82f-2f79-4cd6-b727-0f81230e0837#agent:ab04d3cff4f12baeb","parent":"