resh target session and provide the complete canonical\n   transcript as bootstrap context.\n\n## Adapter contract\n\nEach adapter must declare:\n\n- transcript discovery and incremental cursor semantics;\n- how it identifies completed versus partial turns;\n- role/content/tool-call normalization rules;\n- repository/session identity extraction;\n- known omissions and safe failure behavior.\n\nAdapters are readers first. Writing fabricated provider-native sessions may be\nexplored as an optional, version-pinned optimization but is not required for a\nfunctional bridge and must never be the only recovery path.\n\nThe first Claude adapter should evaluate a pinned integration with an existing\nlocal transcript extractor rather than reimplementing its format parser. The\nwrapper still owns an incremental cursor and must tolerate schema changes and\nincomplete final lines.\n\n## Rehydration\n\nThe target adapter receives canonical events in order and constructs the\nsmallest supported bootstrap mechanism: an initial prompt, a local transcript\nfile plus an instruction to read it, or another documented import surface.\nThe UI must say that the target is a new rehydrated session. It must preserve\nliteral content, avoid silently summarizing, and report context-size limits\nbefore launch.\n\n## CLI UX proposal\n\nAn executable shim may intercept familiar forms such as `claude --resume` and\noffer a merged picker. Selecting a native Claude conversation delegates to\nClaude. Selecting a Codex-origin conversation launches Claude through the\nrehydration path instead. Equivalent wrappers can serve other supported CLIs.\n\nDefault listings show only the current user's records that are compatible with\nthe checked-out code. Future cross-user mode expands the list with clear author\nand code-state labels.\n\n## Risks\n\nNative formats can change without notice; transcript content can include\nsecrets; full histories consume substantial context; terminal processes can\ncrash mid-turn. The MVP must retain raw incremental capture, present partial\ncapture honestly, and provide redaction/local-only controls before any\nautomatic sharing is enabled.\n","filePath":"/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/turnbridge/docs/WIP_TECHNICAL_DESIGN.md","numLines":63,"startLine":1,"totalLines":63},"type":"text"},"type":"user","userType":"external","uuid":"04396569-0863-47d1-ada5-3c7fe8c54837","version":"2.1.214"},"format":"claude-code-jsonl/1"},"recorded_at":"2026-08-11T11:07:26.295Z","schema":"conversation-ledger/v1"}
{"actor":{"type":"system"},"content":{"blocks":[{"content":"1\t# WIP technical design\n2\t\n3\t**Status:** exploratory; no compatibility promises.\n4\t\n5\t## Scope\n6\t\n7\tConversation Ledger will define a canonical append-only event format plus a local,\n8\tGit-backed storage protocol. It must preserve exact visible content while\n9\tsupporting efficient indexes and later derived views.\n10\t\n11\t## Canonical objects\n12\t\n13\tAn `EvidenceEvent` is immutable and has:\n14\t\n15\t- `id`, `schema_version`, and content hash;\n16\t- `kind` (`conversation_turn`, `decision`, `document`, `annotation`,\n17\t  `redaction`, or `supersession`);\n18\t- `occurred_at` and `recorded_at` timestamps;\n19\t- `actor` and `producer` provenance;\n20\t- a content reference and media type;\n21\t- repository context: repository identity, branch, `HEAD` SHA, worktree ID,\n22\t  and optional dirty-worktree fingerprint;\n23\t- optional links to related events.\n24\t\n25\tConversation turns preserve visible roles, textual content, tool calls, and\n26\ttool results as supplied by their capture adapter. The source-native payload\n27\tmay be retained as an opaque, versioned attachment for lossless export. Hidden\n28\treasoning is neither requested nor represented.\n29\t\n30\tAn append-only `Conversation` manifest provides ordering and identifies the\n31\tsource CLI's session ID. Derived data must remain separately identifiable from\n32\traw captured events.\n33\t\n34\t## Storage proposal\n35\t\n36\tThe primary candidate is Git objects plus a dedicated notes ref such as\n37\t`refs/notes/conversation-ledger`:\n38\t\n39\t1. Canonical event payloads are content-addressed blobs.\n40\t2. A compact manifest/index points to those blobs.\n41\t3. Git notes associated with a source commit point to the applicable manifest.\n42\t4. Events created against uncommitted work use the current `HEAD` plus a\n43\t   worktree/diff fingerprint in their context.\n44\t\n45\tThis keeps the working tree and `git status` clean, unlike tracked transcript\n46\tfiles. It also avoids a separately checked-out data branch. Fetch/push support\n47\tfor the notes ref will be explicit and opt-in.\n48\t\n49\tThe exact ref layout, garbage-collection rules, and multi-worktree behavior\n50\tare open questions.\n51\t\n52\t## API direction\n53\t\n54\tThe first library/CLI boundary should expose:\n55\t\n56\t- append an immutable event or conversation turn;\n57\t- read a conversation in stable order;\n58\t- enumerate records by repository context, author, source, and ancestry;\n59\t- attach annotations, redactions, and supersession relationships;\n60\t- import/export a complete canonical conversation without data loss;\n61\t- an adapter cursor/checkpoint API for incremental capture.\n62\t\n63\tQuery ranking, semantic search, agent-facing synthesis, and vendor-native\n64\tsession fabrication are explicitly out of scope here.\n65\t\n66\t## Privacy and integrity\n67\t\n68\tVisible tool output can contain secrets. Capture must support exclusion rules,\n69\tredaction events, local-only storage, and clearly distinguish captured content\n70\tfrom derived metadata. Content hashes should make accidental mutation\n71\tdetectable; redaction removes access through a new manifest rather than\n72\tpretending the original event never existed. The retention and remote-sharing\n73\tpolicy must be configured by the repository owner.\n74\t","tool_use_id":"toolu_01Uf5Pu7tAQmXitHrm1AQaGe","type":"tool_result"}],"role":"user"},"context":{"branch":"main","cwd":"/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/conversation-ledger","head":"de79e501289e2e19946780867779ef465ead2124","repo":"git@github.com:evintunador/conversation-ledger.git"},"conversation":{"id":"claude-code:700cd82f-2f79-4cd6-b727-0f81230e0837#agent:a9629fb6e9ebc4372","parent":"claude-code:700cd82f-2f79-4cd6-b727-0f81230e0837","seq":24},"id":"ev1-b91d83fd6b5bda1f1bc1148a780571cb77707f96838332b204835d68248e1206","kind":"conversation_turn","occurred_at":"2026-07-18T22:4