istantUUID":"539b2447-0b4c-4208-948c-1c0848fe40df","timestamp":"2026-07-18T22:41:19.634Z","toolUseResult":{"file":{"content":"# WIP technical design\n\n**Status:** exploratory; no compatibility promises.\n\n## Scope\n\nConversation Ledger will define a canonical append-only event format plus a local,\nGit-backed storage protocol. It must preserve exact visible content while\nsupporting efficient indexes and later derived views.\n\n## Canonical objects\n\nAn `EvidenceEvent` is immutable and has:\n\n- `id`, `schema_version`, and content hash;\n- `kind` (`conversation_turn`, `decision`, `document`, `annotation`,\n  `redaction`, or `supersession`);\n- `occurred_at` and `recorded_at` timestamps;\n- `actor` and `producer` provenance;\n- a content reference and media type;\n- repository context: repository identity, branch, `HEAD` SHA, worktree ID,\n  and optional dirty-worktree fingerprint;\n- optional links to related events.\n\nConversation turns preserve visible roles, textual content, tool calls, and\ntool results as supplied by their capture adapter. The source-native payload\nmay be retained as an opaque, versioned attachment for lossless export. Hidden\nreasoning is neither requested nor represented.\n\nAn append-only `Conversation` manifest provides ordering and identifies the\nsource CLI's session ID. Derived data must remain separately identifiable from\nraw captured events.\n\n## Storage proposal\n\nThe primary candidate is Git objects plus a dedicated notes ref such as\n`refs/notes/conversation-ledger`:\n\n1. Canonical event payloads are content-addressed blobs.\n2. A compact manifest/index points to those blobs.\n3. Git notes associated with a source commit point to the applicable manifest.\n4. Events created against uncommitted work use the current `HEAD` plus a\n   worktree/diff fingerprint in their context.\n\nThis keeps the working tree and `git status` clean, unlike tracked transcript\nfiles. It also avoids a separately checked-out data branch. Fetch/push support\nfor the notes ref will be explicit and opt-in.\n\nThe exact ref layout, garbage-collection rules, and multi-worktree behavior\nare open questions.\n\n## API direction\n\nThe first library/CLI boundary should expose:\n\n- append an immutable event or conversation turn;\n- read a conversation in stable order;\n- enumerate records by repository context, author, source, and ancestry;\n- attach annotations, redactions, and supersession relationships;\n- import/export a complete canonical conversation without data loss;\n- an adapter cursor/checkpoint API for incremental capture.\n\nQuery ranking, semantic search, agent-facing synthesis, and vendor-native\nsession fabrication are explicitly out of scope here.\n\n## Privacy and integrity\n\nVisible tool output can contain secrets. Capture must support exclusion rules,\nredaction events, local-only storage, and clearly distinguish captured content\nfrom derived metadata. Content hashes should make accidental mutation\ndetectable; redaction removes access through a new manifest rather than\npretending the original event never existed. The retention and remote-sharing\npolicy must be configured by the repository owner.\n","filePath":"/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/conversation-ledger/docs/WIP_TECHNICAL_DESIGN.md","numLines":74,"startLine":1,"totalLines":74},"type":"text"},"type":"user","userType":"external","uuid":"1c380025-e3dd-437a-99a1-7ca1bf1e4846","version":"2.1.214"},"format":"claude-code-jsonl/1"},"recorded_at":"2026-08-11T11:07:26.145Z","schema":"conversation-ledger/v1"}
{"actor":{"type":"system"},"content":{"blocks":[{"content":"1\t# WIP technical design\n2\t\n3\t**Status:** exploratory; this is not yet an agent decision engine.\n4\t\n5\t## Evidence model\n6\t\n7\tIntent Recall consumes immutable events from Conversation Ledger and builds derived,\n8\tversioned indexes. Raw evidence always remains addressable. Derived claims must\n9\treference the exact event IDs and excerpts from which they were made.\n10\t\n11\tThe initial evidence classes are:\n12\t\n13\t- human requests and clarifications from visible conversations;\n14\t- accepted/rejected decisions and their chronology;\n15\t- specifications and documentation;\n16\t- tests and code, linked as implementation artifacts rather than treated as\n17\t  unquestioned intent.\n18\t\n19\t## Retrieval flow\n20\t\n21\tGiven a task, file, symbol, behavior, or question, Lens should:\n22\t\n23\t1. Resolve repository/code-state context.\n24\t2. Retrieve relevant raw evidence through lexical, structural, and eventually\n25\t   semantic indexes.\n26\t3. Group evidence by topic and chronology.\n27\t4. Detect explicit supersession or contradiction relationships.\n28\t5. Return a bounded evidence packet with citations, uncertainty, and an\n29\t   invitation to inspect the original material.\n30\t\n31\tAn agent-facing response must separate `evidence`, `inference`, and\n32\t`unresolved_questions`. It must never present a model-generated reconstruction\n33\tas a direct historical quote.\n34\t\n35\t## Structured intent (future)\n36\t\n37\tStructured claims may eventually model actors, requested behaviors,\n38\tconstraints, acceptance criteria, scope, and supersession. They are derived\n39\tannotations, not replacements for raw conversations. Each claim needs source\n40\tlinks, confidence, extractor/version provenance, and a review/correction path.\n41\t\n42\t## Open questions\n43\t\n44\t- What source-link granularity is useful: turn, paragraph, sentence, or span?\n45\t- How should current user instructions interact with contradictory history?\n46\t- Which sensitive evidence may be indexed or shown to a model?\n47\t- How should branches, rebases, and renamed symbols affect relevance?\n48\t- What evaluation set can measure faithful retrieval without rewarding\n49\t  persuasive but unsupported synthesis?\n50\t","tool_use_id":"toolu_01AUhh5HMpGPNYRsQDKN4B1q","type":"tool_result"}],"role":"user"},"context":{"branch":"main","cwd":"/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/conversation-ledger","head":"de79e501289e2e19946780867779ef465ead2124","repo":"git@github.com:evintunador/conversation-ledger.git"},"conversation":{"id":"claude-code:700cd82f-2f79-4cd6-b727-0f81230e0837#agent:ab04d3cff4f12baeb","parent":"claude-code:700cd82f-2f79-4cd6-b727-0f81230e0837","seq":23},"id":"ev1-0b6b4e69603269efdf85eb2a7bc275d87caa6f860165cad684a8acbe34c8b486","kind":"conversation_turn","occurred_at":"2026-07-18T22:12:58.235Z","producer":{"session_id":"700cd82f-2f79-4cd6-b727-0f81230e0837","source":"claude-code","source_version":"2.1.214","tool":"cledger","version":"0.20.0"},"raw":{"data":{"agentId":"ab04d3cff4f12baeb","cwd":"/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/conversation-ledger","entrypoint":"cli","gitBranch":"main","isSidechain":true,"message":{"content":[{"content":"1\t# WIP technical design\n2\t\n3\t**Status:** exploratory; this is not yet an agent decision engine.\n4\t\n5\t## Evidence model\n6\t\n7\tIntent Recall consumes immutable events from Conversation Ledger and builds derived,\n8\tversioned indexes. Raw evidence always remains addressable. Derived claims must\n9\treference the exact event IDs and excerpts from which they were made.\n10\t\n11\tThe initial evidence classes are:\n12\t\n13\t- human requests and clarifications from visible conversations;\n14\t- accepted/rejected decisions and their chronology;\n15\t- specifications and documentation;\n16\t- tests and code, linked as implementation artifacts rather than treated as\n17\t  unquestioned intent.\n18\t\n19\t## Retrieval flow\n20\t\n21\tGiven a task, file, symbol, behavior, or question, Lens should:\n22\t\n23\t1. Resolve repository/code-state context.\n24\t2. Retrieve relevant raw evidence through lexical, structural, and eventually\n25\t   semantic indexes.\n26\t3. Group evidence by topic and chronology.\n27\t4. Detect explicit supersession or contradiction relationships.\n28\t5. Return a bounded evidence packet with citations, uncertainty, and an\n29\t   invitation to inspect the original material.\n30\t\n31\tAn agent-facing response must separate `evidence`, `inference`, and\n32\t`unresolved_questions`. It must never present a model-generated reconstruction\n33\tas a direct historical quote.\n34\t\n35\t## Structured intent (future)\n36\t\n37\tStructured claims may eventually model actors, requested behaviors,\n38\tconstraints, acceptance criteria, scope, and supersession. They are derived\n39\tannotations, not replacements for raw conversations. Each claim needs source\n40\tlinks, confidence, extractor/version provenance, and a review/correction path.\n41\t\n42\t## Open questions\n43\t\n44\t- What source-link granularity is useful: turn, paragraph, sentence, or span?\n45\t- How should current user instructions interact with contradictory history?\n46\t- Which sensitive evidence may be indexed or shown to a model?\n47\t- How should branches, rebases, and renamed symbols affect relevance?\n48\t- What evaluation set can measure faithful retrieval without rewarding\n49\t  persuasive but unsupported synthesis?\n50\t","tool_use_id":"toolu_01AUhh5HMpGPNYRsQDKN4B1q","type":"tool_result"}],"role":"user"},"parentUuid":"ee749538-bc6b-4726-986b-0014358c0985","promptId":"c4c659c5-32f9-448e-8ca7-bbe19d257601","sessionId":"700cd82f-2f79-4cd6-b727-0f81230e0837","slug":"quirky-shimmying-spark","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"ee749538-bc6b-4726-986b-0014358c0985","timestamp":"2026-07-18T22:12:58.235Z","toolUseResult":{"file":{"content":"# WIP technical design\n\n**Status:** exploratory; this is not yet an agent decision engine.\n\n## Evidence model\n\nIntent Recall consumes immutable events from Conversation Ledger and builds derived,\nversioned indexes. Raw evidence always remains addressable. Derived claims must\nreference the exact event IDs and excerpts from which they were made.\n\nThe initial evidence classes are:\n\n- human requests and clarifications from visible conversations;\n- accepted/rejected decisions and their chronology;\n- specifications and documentation;\n- tests and code, linked as implementation artifacts rather than treated as\n  unquestioned intent.\n\n## Retrieval flow\n\nGiven a task, file, symbol, behavior, or question, Lens should:\n\n1. Resolve repository/code-state context.\n2. Retrieve relevant raw evidence through lexical, structural, and eventually\n   semantic indexes.\n3. Group evidence by topic and chronology.\n4. Detect explicit supersession or contradiction relationships.\n5. Return a bounded evidence packet with citations, uncertainty, and an\n   invitation to inspect the original material.\n\nAn agent-facing response must separate `evidence`, `inference`, and\n`unresolved_questions`. It must never present a model-generated reconstruction\nas a direct historical quote.\n\n## Structured intent (future)\n\nStructured claims may eventually model actors, requested behaviors,\nconstraints, acceptance criteria, scope, and supersession. They are derived\nannotations, not replacements for raw conversations. Each claim needs source\nlinks, confidence, extractor/version provenance, and a review/correction path.\n\n## Open questions\n\n- What source-link granularity is useful: turn, paragraph, sentence, or span?\n- How should current user instructions interact with contradictory history?\n- Which sensitive evidence may be indexed or shown to a model?\n- How should branches, rebases, and renamed symbols affect relevance?\n- What evaluation set can measure faithful retrieval without rewarding\n  persuasive but unsupported synthesis?\n","fi