reasoning)\n43\t  cledger sync [--remote R] [--push|--fetch] [--no-scan] [--paranoid]\n44\t                                           fetch/merge/push of the ledger ref;\n45\t                                           push is gated by a secret scan unless --no-scan\n46\t  cledger transport-push [remote]         pre-push hook entrypoint (installed automatically):\n47\t                                           pushes the ledger ref alongside git push; scan findings\n48\t                                           hold back only the ledger unless transport.strict\n49\t  cledger scan [--all|--rev R] [--paranoid]   scan local events for potential secrets (CI-friendly:\n50\t                                           exits 1 if any finding, 0 otherwise); default scope is\n51\t                                           every local event, --rev restricts by reachability\n52\t  cledger allow <fingerprint...>          mark scan finding fingerprint(s) as known false positives\n53\t  cledger redact <event-id-prefix> (--pattern REGEX | --all) [--reason TEXT]\n54\t                                           rewrite an existing event to remove a secret, keeping its\n55\t                                           id stable, and squash local notes history if unpushed\n56\t  cledger re-anchor [--apply] [--target R] [--no-forge]\n57\t                                           detect branches squash-merged/rewritten onto the remote\n58\t                                           default branch and map their conversations to the\n59\t                                           surviving commits (dry-run by default; exact matches\n60\t                                           also auto-apply on read unless reanchor.auto is false).\n61\t                                           Inexact cases get evidence-ranked suggestions — forge PR\n62\t                                           metadata via your own gh session, commit-message\n63\t                                           corroboration