{"actor":{"type":"system"},"content":{"blocks":[{"content":"70\tThe note body is JSONL: one canonical-JSON (sorted-keys) event per line,\n71\tlexicographically sorted, unique.\n72\t\n73\tWhy this shape:\n74\t\n75\t1. **Branch-tied by construction.** Events anchor to `HEAD` at capture time,\n76\t   so conversations ride the commit DAG: merging a branch makes its commits —\n77\t   and therefore their conversations — reachable from the target branch with\n78\t   no sync machinery. `cledger log` scopes to the current branch via\n79\t   `git rev-list` reachability.\n80\t2. **GC-safe, nothing outside git.** All content lives inline in the note\n81\t   blob, reachable from the ref. No orphan data branches, no pointers to\n82\t   stores outside the repository.\n83\t3. **Conflict-free concurrency.** Deterministic serialization + sorted unique\n84\t   lines mean git's `cat_sort_uniq` notes merge strategy (configured per-ref\n85\t   at first append) unions concurrent appends cleanly — the same mechanism\n86\t   git-bug and git-appraise rely on.\n87\t4. **Clean working tree.** Notes never appear in `git status`; sharing is\n88\t   the fetch → `git notes merge -s cat_sort_uniq` → push of that single\n89\t   ref, run by the default-on transport hooks or explicitly via `cledger\n90\t   sync` (the E scan gates the push either way — see \"Transport\").\n91\t\n92\tEvents captured before the first commit exists (unborn `HEAD`) queue in\n93\t`.git/conversation-ledger/pending.jsonl` and flush into the first real\n94\tanchor. Everything under `.git/conversation-ledger/` (pending queue, adapter\n95\tcursors, lock) is local, rebuildable state — never the record of truth.\n96\t\n97\t### Known limitation: squash merges\n98\t\n99\tA squash merge discards the source branch's commits, so their conversations\n100\tremain in the ledger (notes are enumerable regardless of reachability;\n101\t`cledger log --all` sees them) but drop out of the target branch's\n102\treachability view. A future `re-anchor` operation is the intended fix.\n103\t\n104\t## Transport\n105\t\n106\tDefault-on, wired by the first capture in a repo (`ensureTransport`, run on\n107\tevery append as cheap re-checks so a remote added later still gets covered;\n108\tnever throws — it runs inside capture):\n109\t\n110\t- **Push half.** A `pre-push` hook calls `cledger transport-push <remote>`,\n111\t  which pushes the ledger ref gated by the layer-E scan. Policy: a finding\n112\t  holds back *only the ledger* — secrets never leave the machine, but a\n113\t  false positive never blocks shipping code; `{\"transport\": {\"strict\":\n114\t  true}}` escalates to aborting the entire push. Any other failure warns\n115\t  and lets the push proceed. Installation is chain-safe: append to an\n116\t  existing shell hook, back off with a one-time warning when\n117\t  `core.hooksPath` or a non-shell hook owns the file. The hook script\n118\t  embeds the installing cledger's absolute node+cli.js path (PATH fallback\n119\t  in the script), treats \"cledger gone\" as success, and a\n120\t  `CLEDGER_INTERNAL` env guard (set by `sync` around its own push) stops\n121\t  the ledger push from re-triggering the hook.\n122\t- **Fetch half.** A `+refs/notes/conversation-ledger:refs/notes/\n123\t  cledger-incoming` refspec on `origin` makes plain `git fetch`/`git pull`\n124\t  stage the remote's ref; `absorbIncoming` folds the staging ref into the\n125\t  local ref lazily at read time (every `readEvents`) via the same\n126\t  `cat_sort_uniq` union — absorption can only add events, and the local\n127\t  ref is never force-overwritten. `cledger sync`'s fetch phase uses the\n128\t  identical staging path.\n129\t- **Opt-out.** `{\"transport\": {\"hook\": false, \"fetchRefspec\": false}}`","tool_use_id":"toolu_017n8TJRewmtbwntUgQFvuMW","type":"tool_result"}],"role":"user"},"context":{"branch":"main","cwd":"/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/conversation-ledger","head":"de79e501289e2e19946780867779ef465ead2124","repo":"git