ace-only — plain `ssh 100.x` never routes anywhere. The prior setup already solved this correctly with `/home/root/bin/tssh`, which proxies through `tailscale nc` as an OpenSSH `ProxyCommand`, using the real OpenSSH client at `/opt/bin/ssh` (not the tablet's built-in Dropbear `ssh`, which can't parse modern `openssh-key-v1`-format keys at all — that's a real, confirmed Dropbear limitation, not a config issue).\\n41\\t  - The only actually stale thing was `/home/root/bin/mac`, a one-line shortcut hardcoded to the old MacBook Air's Tailscale IP (`100.72.225.106`). Updated it to this Mac's Tailscale IP (`100.105.108.44`). Verified end-to-end: `mac \\\"echo ok\\\"` from the tablet works.\\n42\\t  - Remote Login (SSH server) enabled on this Mac (was off by default on the fresh install).\\n43\\t  - Dead end explored and reverted: temporarily restricted this Mac's sshd `KexAlgorithms` to non-quantum-safe algorithms chasing a red herring — reverted, back to full defaults.\\n44\\t\\n45\\t## 5. Expose ds4 as a semi-public API for the reMarkable (and friends), only while the laptop is plugged in\\n46\\t\\n47\\t- **Goal:** let the reMarkable tablet — and some external people (\\\"friends\\\") — hit the local `ds4-server` (DeepSeek V4 Flash, already downloaded/working) over the network, but not have it running unconditionally or fully open to the world.\\n48\\t- [ ] Decide exposure mechanism — Tailscale is already installed, two real options:\\n49\\t  - **Tailscale Serve** — private to devices on the tailnet only; \\\"friends\\\" would need to be invited onto the tailnet (simplest, most secure, but not truly public)\\n50\\t  - **Tailscale Funnel** — actually publicly reachable over HTTPS from the open internet, no tailnet invite needed for friends, but wider exposure surface\\n51\\t- [ ] Decide access control — \\\"friends\\\" implies more than one external user; given DeepSeek V4 Flash inference is resource-heavy, probably wants an API key / allowlist rather than wide-open access.\\n52\\t- [ ] Make it conditional on AC power (\\\"periods when my laptop is plugged in\\\") — likely a `launchd` job (or a script triggered by `pmset -g batt` power-source changes) that starts `ds4-server` + the Tailscale Serve/Funnel when plugged in and stops them on battery, rather than running 24/7.\\n53\\t\"}]}\n{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":\"let's start working on the iCloud cleanup. you can see in i recently moved contents inside the repos/ and Projects folders (those might be inside Documents/ or something i forget) from icloud into here, so those can be deleted off the bat. the main initial targets for cleanup are going to be my desktop & downloads folders. please go through teh files and draw them into categories, including \\\"unknown\\\", and provide recommendations/options for where to move them to elsewhere on my icloud.\"}\n\n=== an assistant message (elided text) ===\n{\"model\":\"claude-fable-5\",\"id\":\"msg_011Cd72E1XvfSTXAgoAXwPSL\",\"type\":\"message\",\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"thinking\",\"thinking\":\"\",\"signature\":\"\"}],\"stop_reason\":\"tool_use\",\"stop_sequence\":null,\"stop_details\":null,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":2,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":7995,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":12572,\"output_tokens\":72,\"server_tool_use\":{\"web_search_requests\":0,\"web_fetch_requests\":0},\"service_tier\":\"standard\",\"cache_creation\":{\"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens\":7995,\"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens\":0},\"inference_geo\":\"not_available\",\"iterations\":[{\"input_tokens\":2,\"output_tokens\":72,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":12572,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":7995,\"cache_creation\":{\"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens\":0,\"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens\":7995},\"type\":\"message\"}],\"speed\":\"standard\"},\"diagnostics\":null}\n{\"model\":\"claude-fable-5\",\"id\":\"msg_011Cd72E1XvfSTXAgoAXwPSL\",\"type\":\"message\",\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"id\":\"toolu_011e8nRtXGKyoTJQYasAQtLc\",\"name\"