{"actor":{"type":"system"},"content":{"blocks":[{"content":"Web search results for query: \"Amp CLI hooks notify lifecycle events configuration\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"describe-lifecycle-hooks — AWS CLI 2.33.13 Command Reference\",\"url\":\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/cli/latest/reference/autoscaling/describe-lifecycle-hooks.html\"},{\"title\":\"Owner’s Manual - Amp\",\"url\":\"https://ampcode.com/manual\"},{\"title\":\"put-lifecycle-hook — AWS CLI 2.1.29 Command Reference\",\"url\":\"https://awscli.amazonaws.com/v2/documentation/api/2.1.29/reference/autoscaling/put-lifecycle-hook.html\"},{\"title\":\"put-lifecycle-hook — AWS CLI 2.35.23 Command Reference\",\"url\":\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/cli/latest/reference/autoscaling/put-lifecycle-hook.html\"},{\"title\":\"put-lifecycle-hook — AWS CLI 2.4.19 Command Reference\",\"url\":\"https://awscli.amazonaws.com/v2/documentation/api/2.4.19/reference/autoscaling/put-lifecycle-hook.html\"},{\"title\":\"put-lifecycle-hook — AWS CLI 2.8.7 Command Reference\",\"url\":\"https://awscli.amazonaws.com/v2/documentation/api/2.8.7/reference/autoscaling/put-lifecycle-hook.html\"},{\"title\":\"put-lifecycle-event-hook-execution-status — AWS CLI 2.25.10 Command Reference\",\"url\":\"https://awscli.amazonaws.com/v2/documentation/api/latest/reference/deploy/put-lifecycle-event-hook-execution-status.html\"},{\"title\":\"put-lifecycle-hook — AWS CLI 2.1.30 Command Reference\",\"url\":\"https://awscli.amazonaws.com/v2/documentation/api/2.1.30/reference/autoscaling/put-lifecycle-hook.html\"},{\"title\":\"Add lifecycle hooks to your Auto Scaling group - Amazon EC2 Auto Scaling\",\"url\":\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/autoscaling/ec2/userguide/adding-lifecycle-hooks.html\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I found relevant information about Amp CLI hooks and lifecycle events. Here are the key findings:\n\n## Amp CLI Hooks and Lifecycle Events\n\nThe `session.start` event fires when Amp starts a thread session, such as when the user sends the first message in a new thread or opens/switches to an existing thread. There is no session.end event.\n\n### Configuring Hooks\n\nYou can register hooks using the plugin API, for example: `amp.on('session.start', async (event, ctx) => { await ctx.ui.notify(...) })`\n\nThe `tool.call` event fires before a tool runs, and you can return allow to run the tool, reject-and-continue to block it and let the agent continue, modify to change the input, or synthesize to provide a result without running the tool.\n\n### Execute Mode and Plugins\n\nIf your plugins rely on the agent.start and agent.end lifecycle events, use the `--plugin-ready-timeout` flag to make execute mode wait for plugins to become ready before running the turn.\n\nThe Amp CLI supports plugin-based event hooks that allow you to listen to and respond to various lifecycle events during the operation of the CLI.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks.","tool_use_id":"toolu_01BzdddXZFRkdAjR8KDY2Rk5","type":"tool_result"}],"role":"user"},"context":{"branch":"main","cwd":"/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/conversation-ledger","head":"de79e501289e2e19946780867779ef465ead2124","repo":"git@github.com:evintunador/conversation-ledger.git"},"conversation":{"id":"claude-code:700cd82f-2f79-4cd6-b727-0f81230e0837#agent:a4fc099b2ea3fc467","parent":"claude-code:700cd82f-2f79-4cd6-b727-0f81230e0837","seq":77},"id":"ev1-dc499020eec378ebc73163e106fbdd51b7865a404d4e7c284ba58afaa4e967b6","kind":"conversation_turn","occurred_at":"2026-07-18T23:23:58.869Z","producer":{"session_id":"700cd82f-2f79-4cd6-b727-0f81230e0837","source":"claude-code","source_version":"2.1.214","tool":"cledger","version":"0.20.0"},"raw":{"data":{"agentId":"a4fc099b2ea3fc467","cwd":"/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/conversation-ledger","entrypoint":"cli","gitBranch":"main","isSidechain":true,"message":{"content":[{"content":"Web search results for query: \"Amp CLI hooks notify lifecyc