{"actor":{"type":"system"},"content":{"blocks":[{"content":"Web search results for query: \"Amp Sourcegraph CLI session storage local threads hooks 2026\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Amp by Coder Labs | Coder Registry\",\"url\":\"https://registry.coder.com/modules/coder-labs/sourcegraph-amp\"},{\"title\":\"Sourcegraph Amp in 5 minutes - The Good, the Bad and the Ugly\",\"url\":\"https://zoltanbourne.substack.com/p/early-preview-of-amp-the-new-ai-coding\"},{\"title\":\"amp-examples-and-guides/guides/cli/README.md at main · ampcode/amp-examples-and-guides\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/sourcegraph/amp-examples-and-guides/blob/main/guides/cli/README.md\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - ampcode/amp-examples-and-guides · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/sourcegraph/amp-examples-and-guides\"},{\"title\":\"Amp Code Review 2026: Sourcegraph's Autonomous Coding Agent Tested | RockB\",\"url\":\"https://baeseokjae.github.io/posts/amp-code-review-2026/\"},{\"title\":\"sourcegraph/amp\",\"url\":\"https://www.npmjs.com/package/@sourcegraph/amp\"},{\"title\":\"Amp CLI\",\"url\":\"https://www.npmjs.com/package/@sourcegraph/amp/v/0.0.1745121793-7a0270\"},{\"title\":\"Amp by Sourcegraph - Cursor-Alternatives.com\",\"url\":\"https://cursor-alternatives.com/ide-extensions/amp-by-sourcegraph/\"},{\"title\":\"@sourcegraph/amp - npm\",\"url\":\"https://www.npmjs.com/package/@sourcegraph/amp/v/0.0.1744531409-dev\"},{\"title\":\"Amp — CLI for AI Coding (2026) | LLMReference\",\"url\":\"https://www.llmreference.com/agents/amp\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here's what I found about Amp, Sourcegraph's CLI, and session/thread storage:\n\n## Thread Storage and Synchronization\n\nAmp automatically stores all Agent chat threads on Sourcegraph's servers, making them accessible via your account at ampcode.com/threads. Additionally, threads are persistent conversations that maintain context across interactions, and your threads sync to ampcode.com, allowing you to continue conversations across devices.\n\n## Local Storage Alternative\n\nHowever, there has been discussion about local-first storage options. A local-first alternative would be storing threads inside the project directory (e.g. .threads), which would allow teams to version, discard, gitignore or audit conversations as part of the normal workflow.\n\n## CLI and Features\n\nYou can set up environment variables including AMP_SETTINGS_FILE for custom settings location in automated workflows, GitHub pipelines, or any environment where an executable can run. Amp comes with built-in tools for coding tasks and can be extended with custom MCP (Model Context Protocol) servers.\n\n## Thread Management Commands\n\nAmp offers CLI commands for thread management including: creating new threads, continuing existing threads, listing all threads, forking threads, sharing threads, and compacting threads to reduce token usage.\n\nThe search results indicate that as of 2026, Amp primarily syncs threads to Sourcegraph's servers rather than storing them locally by default, though there's been community interest in local storage options.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks.","tool_use_id":"toolu_01DE7VRNq8MgwAEuoZLGvMHg","type":"tool_result"}],"role":"user"},"context":{"branch":"main","cwd":"/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/conversation-ledger","head":"de79e501289e2e19946780867779ef465ead2124","repo":"git@github.com:evintunador/conversation-ledger.git"},"conversation":{"id":"claude-code:700cd82f-2f79-4cd6-b727-0f81230e0837#agent:a4fc099b2ea3fc467","parent":"claude-code:700cd82f-2f79-4cd6-b727-0f81230e0837","seq":66},"id":"ev1-c73ddff38a0a6871622ad7b48ccc8ced1f06a37dccc0616c7590e98cd2b6901a","kind":"conversation_turn","occurred_at":"2026-07-18T23:23:37.034Z","producer":{"session_id":"700cd82f-2f79-4cd6-b727-0f81230e0837","source":"claude-code","source_version":"2.1.214","tool":"cledger","version":"0.20.0"},"raw":{"data":{"agentId":"a4fc099b2ea3fc467","cw