in settings.json\n\nHooks are created by adding a hooks block to a settings file. To add, modify, or remove hooks, edit your settings JSON directly or ask Claude to make the change.\n\n## Desktop App Support\n\nThe IDE extensions read the same settings.json tree as the CLI, so permissions, hooks, and mcpServers apply uniformly. However, there's an important distinction: Claude Code supports lifecycle hooks configured in ~/.claude/settings.json (UserPromptSubmit, Stop, PreToolUse, PostToolUse, etc.), but Cowork (a related product) does not fire these hooks.\n\n## Hook Types and Configuration\n\nIn the Builder, pick a lifecycle event, set a matcher, and add one or more handlers (command, http, mcp_tool, prompt, or agent) to generate the hooks block. As of July 1, 2026, the reference documents 30 hook events.\n\n## Key Events\n\nNearly every production setup is built from five: PreToolUse, PostToolUse, UserPromptSubmit, SessionStart, and Stop.\n\nFor the most current and detailed information about hooks support, you can refer to the official Claude Code documentation at code.claude.com/docs/en/hooks.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks.","tool_use_id":"toolu_016axoTkBTVoDWMcELHHqmg6","type":"tool_result"}],"role":"user"},"context":{"branch":"main","cwd":"/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/conversation-ledger","head":"de79e501289e2e19946780867779ef465ead2124","repo":"git@github.com:evintunador/conversation-ledger.git"},"conversation":{"id":"claude-code:700cd82f-2f79-4cd6-b727-0f81230e0837#agent:a4fc099b2ea3fc467","parent":"claude-code:700cd82f-2f79-4cd6-b727-0f81230e0837","seq":30},"id":"ev1-faf61958e115fa405559684702b449b2a72015bbb30da930958d1c9c52611325","kind":"conversation_turn","occurred_at":"2026-07-18T23:22:31.817Z","producer":{"session_id":"700cd82f-2f79-4cd6-b727-0f81230e0837","source":"claude-code","source_version":"2.1.214","tool":"cledger","version":"0.20.0"},"raw":{"data":{"agentId":"a4f