{"actor":{"type":"system"},"content":{"blocks":[{"content":"Web search results for query: \"Claude Code ~/.claude/projects transcript jsonl session storage /resume\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Manage sessions - Claude Code Docs\",\"url\":\"https://code.claude.com/docs/en/sessions\"},{\"title\":\"Session Storage - ClaudeWorld\",\"url\":\"https://claude-world.com/tutorials/s16-session-storage/\"},{\"title\":\"How to resume, search, and manage Claude Code conversations | @kentgigger\",\"url\":\"https://kentgigger.com/posts/claude-code-conversation-history\"},{\"title\":\"How to Recover an Accidentally Closed Claude Code Session\",\"url\":\"https://inventivehq.com/blog/recover-closed-claude-code-session\"},{\"title\":\"Claude Code History: Where It's Stored & How to Restore It\",\"url\":\"https://www.codeagentswarm.com/en/guides/claude-code-history-complete-guide\"},{\"title\":\"Exploring Conversation History | CodeSignal Learn\",\"url\":\"https://codesignal.com/learn/courses/foundation-getting-started-with-claude-code/lessons/exploring-conversation-history\"},{\"title\":\"Session management - Claude Code\",\"url\":\"https://jackdog668-claude-code.mintlify.app/usage/session-management\"},{\"title\":\"Claude Code JSONL transcript format explained\",\"url\":\"https://claude-dev.tools/docs/jsonl-format\"},{\"title\":\"cleanupPeriodDays: 0 silently disables all transcript persistence (docs say it disables cleanup) · Issue #23710 · anthropics/claude-code\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/anthropics/claude-code/issues/23710\"}]\n\n## Search Results\n\nI found comprehensive information about Claude Code's session storage, transcripts, and resume functionality. Here's what the search revealed:\n\n### Session Storage Location\nBy default, transcripts are stored as JSONL at ~/.claude/projects/<project>/<session-id>.jsonl, where <project> is your working directory path with non-alphanumeric characters replaced by -.\n\n### Transcript Format\nEach line is a JSON object for a message, tool use, or metadata entry. Each .jsonl file contains one JSON object per line. Each line is a message — user turn, assistant turn, tool call, or system event — appended as the session progresses.\n\n### Resume Functionality\nWhen we use /resume, Claude identifies our current project, lists all .jsonl files in the corresponding projects/ folder, and sorts them by modification time. When we select a conversation, Claude loads that entire .jsonl file sequentially, reconstructing the conversation from those JSON events.\n\n### Important Limitations\nThe entry format is internal to Claude Code and changes between versions, so scripts that parse these files directly can break on any release. To build on session data, use /export or the script interfaces instead.\n\n### Resuming Sessions\nClaude Code scopes conversations to the project directory they were created in, so you must cd back into that exact folder before running claude --continue or claude --resume.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks.","tool_use_id":"toolu_011TV5192sZ9c6FGZ7VxXW9c","type":"tool_result"}],"role":"user"},"context":{"branch":"main","cwd":"/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/conversation-ledger","head":"de79e501289e2e19946780867779ef465ead2124","repo":"git@github.com:evintunador/conversation-ledger.git"},"conversation":{"id":"claude-code:700cd82f-2f79-4cd6-b727-0f81230e0837#agent:af424cc63295b8016","parent":"claude-code:700cd82f-2f79-4cd6-b727-0f81230e0837","seq":15},"id":"ev1-9bbd99f4581932f74731b3d0c248251471f954db68de207e702d9a4ee7dc4fca","kind":"conversation_turn","occurred_at":"2026-07-18T22:13:16.114Z","producer":{"session_id":"700cd82f-2f79-4cd6-b727-0f81230e0837","source":"claude-code","source_version":"2.1.214","tool":"cledger","version":"0.20.0"},"raw":{"data":{"agentId":"af424cc63295b8016","cwd":"/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/conversation-ledger","entrypoint":"cli","gitBranch":"main","isSidechain":true,"message"