{"actor":{"type":"system"},"content":{"blocks":[{"content":"Web search results for query: \"Codex IDE extension VS Code local rollout sessions config.toml notify hooks\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Advanced Configuration | ChatGPT Learn\",\"url\":\"https://developers.openai.com/codex/config-advanced\"},{\"title\":\"Configuration Reference | ChatGPT Learn\",\"url\":\"https://developers.openai.com/codex/config-reference\"},{\"title\":\"The Codex IDE Extension: VS Code, JetBrains, and the Hybrid Cloud-Local Workflow | Codex Knowledge Base\",\"url\":\"https://codex.danielvaughan.com/2026/04/01/codex-ide-extension-vs-code-jetbrains/\"},{\"title\":\"A practical guide to OpenAI Codex integrations with VS Code (2026) | eesel AI\",\"url\":\"https://www.eesel.ai/blog/openai-codex-integrations-with-vs-code\"},{\"title\":\"Developer settings | ChatGPT Learn\",\"url\":\"https://developers.openai.com/codex/ide/settings/\"},{\"title\":\"Advanced Configuration | ChatGPT Learn - OpenAI Developers\",\"url\":\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/docs/config-file/config-advanced\"},{\"title\":\"Config basics | ChatGPT Learn\",\"url\":\"https://developers.openai.com/codex/config-basic\"},{\"title\":\"Hooks | ChatGPT Learn\",\"url\":\"https://developers.openai.com/codex/hooks\"},{\"title\":\"codex_hooks do not fire in interactive sessions when configured via repo-local .codex/config.toml · Issue #17532 · openai/codex\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/openai/codex/issues/17532\"},{\"title\":\"How to Integrate Codex CLI with Your IDE | Inventive HQ\",\"url\":\"https://inventivehq.com/knowledge-base/openai/how-to-integrate-with-ide\"}]\n\nBased on the web search results, here's what I found regarding the Codex IDE extension for VS Code and its configuration:\n\n## Configuration Files and Hooks\n\nCodex CLI reads personal defaults from ~/.codex/config.toml, and you can add a .codex/config.toml file to a trusted project or subfolder for project-specific overrides. The CLI and IDE extension share these configuration layers.\n\n## Lifecycle Hooks Configuration\n\nCodex can load lifecycle hooks from either hooks.json files or inline [hooks] tables in config.toml files that sit next to active config layers. Inline TOML hooks use the same event structure as hooks.json, with examples like [[hooks.PreToolUse]] matcher patterns and command hooks with timeout and statusMessage properties.\n\n## Important IDE Extension Limitation\n\nThere's a notable limitation for the IDE extension: Hooks — the experimental hooks engine fires in CLI sessions but not IDE sessions. This means while you can configure hooks in config.toml, they won't execute within the VS Code IDE extension itself, only in CLI sessions.\n\n## Notification and Telemetry Keys\n\nYou should set provider, notification, and telemetry keys in your user-level ~/.codex/config.toml. Additionally, Codex ignores the following keys in project-local .codex/config.toml: openai_base_url, chatgpt_base_url, apps_mcp_product_sku, model_provider, model_providers, notify, profile, profiles, experimental_realtime_ws_base_url, and otel.\n\nThis search revealed that while local config.toml files support notify and hooks configuration, the IDE extension has limited hook support compared to the CLI.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks.","tool_use_id":"toolu_01XL7SWNKGWxU7HjeYyob1qv","type":"tool_result"}],"role":"user"},"context":{"branch":"main","cwd":"/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/conversation-ledger","head":"de79e501289e2e19946780867779ef465ead2124","repo":"git@github.com:evintunador/conversation-ledger.git"},"conversation":{"id":"claude-code:700cd82f-2f79-4cd6-b727-0f81230e0837#agent:a4fc099b2ea3fc467","parent":"claude-code:700cd82f-2f79-4cd6-b727-0f81230e0837","seq":19},"id":"ev1-f8dc16cff2c167b8ea60fc026a19309d51c69de4d83d7c071a236580669f76a1","kind":"conversation_turn","occurred_at":"2026-07-18T23:22:15.590Z","producer":{"session_id":"700cd82f-2f79-4cd6-b727-