{"actor":{"type":"system"},"content":{"blocks":[{"content":"Web search results for query: \"Codex cloud tasks rollout files local disk ~/.codex/sessions cloud environment\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Desktop app stuck in cloud-only mode; local sessions ignored even with `codexCloudAccess=disabled` · Issue #10547 · openai/codex\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/openai/codex/issues/10547\"},{\"title\":\"Codex cloud | ChatGPT Learn\",\"url\":\"https://developers.openai.com/codex/cloud\"},{\"title\":\"Codex CLI Session Lifecycle: Archive, Resume, Fork, and Compact | Codex Knowledge Base\",\"url\":\"https://codex.danielvaughan.com/2026/06/05/codex-cli-session-lifecycle-archive-resume-fork-compact-management/\"},{\"title\":\"Codex cloud | ChatGPT Learn - OpenAI Developers\",\"url\":\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/docs/cloud\"},{\"title\":\"Cloud environments | ChatGPT Learn\",\"url\":\"https://developers.openai.com/codex/cloud/environments\"},{\"title\":\"Cloud environments\",\"url\":\"https://developers.openai.com/codex/cloud/environments.md/\"},{\"title\":\"Codex CLI Guide 2026: Setup, Sandbox, AGENTS.md & MCP\",\"url\":\"https://blakecrosley.com/guides/codex\"},{\"title\":\"Codex Cloud vs Codex Local: When to Run in the Cloud | Codex Knowledge Base\",\"url\":\"https://codex.danielvaughan.com/2026/03/27/codex-cloud-vs-local-when-to-run-in-cloud/\"},{\"title\":\"Codex cloud tasks vs local coding agents: 2026 workflow guide\",\"url\":\"https://techtaek.com/codex-cloud-tasks-vs-local-coding-agents-in-2026-where-background-work-actually-saves-time/\"},{\"title\":\"Cloud Execution Environments | Developer Toolkit\",\"url\":\"https://developertoolkit.ai/en/codex/advanced-techniques/cloud-environments/\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here's information about Codex cloud tasks, rollout files, local disk storage, and cloud environments:\n\n## Session Storage & Rollout Files\n\nSessions are stored as JSONL rollout files at ~/.codex/sessions/YYYY/MM/DD/, following the naming pattern rollout-YYYY-MM-DDTHH-MM-SS-*.jsonl. Each file records the complete conversation trace, including tool invocations and their outputs. This local-first storage model means sessions survive network outages and remain inspectable with standard Unix tools like jq.\n\n## Local vs. Cloud Execution\n\nThe local CLI runs entirely on your machine. When you invoke codex in a terminal, the agent reads your working directory, edits files, and executes commands inside a sandboxed process scoped to that directory. The session is interactive by default — you see output in real time, approve or reject changes, and stay in the loop.\n\nIn contrast, Codex Cloud provisions an isolated container in OpenAI's infrastructure for each task. The agent checks out your GitHub repository, runs dependency setup scripts, and executes code entirely inside that container. You are disconnected from the task by default — you submit it, go do something else, and collect the resulting diff when it's done.\n\n## Cloud Environments\n\nUse environments to control what Codex installs and runs during cloud tasks. For example, you can add dependencies, install tools like linters and formatters, and set environment variables. Codex creates a container from the universal base image (or a cached state) and checks out your repo at the selected branch or commit SHA. Your custom setup script runs with full internet access. This is where you install dependencies, tools, and configure the environment.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks.","tool_use_id":"toolu_019fDK8YfpHhe8UiPwY4Db9n","type":"tool_result"}],"role":"user"},"context":{"branch":"main","cwd":"/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/conversation-ledger","head":"de79e501289e2e19946780867779ef465ead2124","repo":"git@github.com:evintunador/conversation-ledger.git"},"conversation":{"id":"claude-code:700cd82f-2f79-4cd6-b727-0f81230e0837#agent:a4fc099b2ea3fc467","parent":"claude-code:700cd82f-2f79