{"actor":{"type":"system"},"content":{"blocks":[{"content":"Web search results for query: \"Cursor shared chat link Codex CLI session storage rollout jsonl\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Codex CLI Resume, Continue, and Save Chat Explained - Verdent Guides\",\"url\":\"https://www.verdent.ai/guides/codex-cli-resume-continue-save-chat\"},{\"title\":\"How to Resume a Codex CLI Session: codex resume --last | Inventive HQ\",\"url\":\"https://inventivehq.com/knowledge-base/openai/how-to-resume-sessions\"},{\"title\":\"Cross-Surface Session Sync: Resuming Codex Sessions Across CLI, Desktop and Cloud | Codex Knowledge Base\",\"url\":\"https://codex.danielvaughan.com/2026/04/08/cross-surface-session-sync/\"},{\"title\":\"Ability to share conversations from Codex App, Codex extension and Codex CLI · openai/codex · Discussion #13251\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/openai/codex/discussions/13251\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - Dicklesworthstone/coding_agent_session_search: Unified TUI and CLI to index and search your local coding agent session history across 11+ providers (Codex, Claude, Gemini, Cursor, Aider, etc.) · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/Dicklesworthstone/coding_agent_session_search\"},{\"title\":\"Agent Sessions - Session Management for Codex, Claude, OpenCode, Cursor, Copilot, Pi and Antigravity\",\"url\":\"https://jazzyalex.github.io/agent-sessions/\"},{\"title\":\"Session/Rollout Files · openai/codex · Discussion #3827\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/openai/codex/discussions/3827\"},{\"title\":\"Transfer Claude Code Sessions to OpenAI Codex and Gemini — One Command to Sync AI Agent Context | AuthSec Blog\",\"url\":\"https://authsec.ai/blogs/stop-re-explaining-bridge-claude-codex-gemini\"},{\"title\":\"Copy a single Codex session to another machine – Andrea Zonca\",\"url\":\"https://www.zonca.dev/posts/2025-12-16-copy-codex-session\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here's what I found about Cursor shared chat links, Codex CLI session storage, and the JSONL rollout format:\n\n## Session Storage & JSONL Format\n\nEvery Codex CLI session is automatically saved as a JSONL file in ~/.codex/sessions/. More specifically, Codex CLI stores all session transcripts as JSONL files under ~/.codex/sessions/YYYY/MM/DD/ on macOS and Linux, with each session saved as a rollout-*.jsonl file containing the full conversation history, tool calls, and token usage.\n\nEach file contains the full conversation transcript: your prompts, model responses, tool calls, and tool results, timestamped and structured for replay.\n\n## Rollout Files Architecture\n\nJSONL Rollout Files are stored under ~/.codex/sessions/YYYY/MM/DD/ as .jsonl.zst compressed archives, and each file contains the complete event stream for a thread and serves as the source of truth for replay.\n\n## Shared Chat Links (Cursor)\n\nRegarding shared chat links for Cursor, the feature request is for uploading transcripts to cloud storage to allow sharing with team members. Cursor allows this functionality, which is noted as a feature that Codex doesn't currently have in terms of agent use.\n\nThe search results indicate this is an ongoing feature request in the Codex ecosystem, with discussions around implementing shareable conversation links similar to Cursor's capabilities.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks.","tool_use_id":"toolu_01MabudBqymzMLdm4RfYzMJT","type":"tool_result"}],"role":"user"},"context":{"branch":"main","cwd":"/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/conversation-ledger","head":"de79e501289e2e19946780867779ef465ead2124","repo":"git@github.com:evintunador/conversation-ledger.git"},"conversation":{"id":"claude-code:700cd82f-2f79-4cd6-b727-0f81230e0837#agent:af424cc63295b8016","parent":"claude-code:700cd82f-2f79-4cd6-b727-0f81230e0837","seq":17},"id":"ev1-8c526531929e6078b04d9b5c09a0efda6848ee5497d5c203550723ce4293433e","kind":"conversation_turn","occurred_at":"2026-07-18T22:13:17.567Z","producer":{"session_id":