{"actor":{"type":"system"},"content":{"blocks":[{"content":"Web search results for query: \"Dicklesworthstone coding_agent_session_search agent-sessions jazzyalex tools compare\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"GitHub - Dicklesworthstone/coding_agent_session_search: Unified TUI and CLI to index and search your local coding agent session history across 11+ providers (Codex, Claude, Gemini, Cursor, Aider, etc.) · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/Dicklesworthstone/coding_agent_session_search\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - jazzyalex/agent-sessions: Local-first macOS app to browse, search, analyze, and resume supported AI coding-agent session history across Codex, Claude Code, OpenCode, Cursor Agent, Hermes, OpenClaw, Copilot CLI, and more. · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/jazzyalex/agent-sessions\"},{\"title\":\"agent-sessions/README.md at main · jazzyalex/agent-sessions\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/jazzyalex/agent-sessions/blob/main/README.md\"},{\"title\":\"Agent Sessions - Session Management for Codex, Claude ...\",\"url\":\"https://jazzyalex.github.io/agent-sessions/\"},{\"title\":\"jazzyalex / agent-sessions - Hermes Atlas\",\"url\":\"https://hermesatlas.com/projects/jazzyalex/agent-sessions\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - Dicklesworthstone/cross_agent_session_resumer: Resume AI coding sessions across providers: converts Codex, Claude, Gemini, and other session formats through a canonical IR so you can pick up where you left off in any tool · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/Dicklesworthstone/cross_agent_session_resumer\"},{\"title\":\"Show HN: Coding Agent Session Search (Cass) | Hacker News\",\"url\":\"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=46130481\"},{\"title\":\"Releases · Dicklesworthstone/cross_agent_session_resumer\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/Dicklesworthstone/cross_agent_session_resumer/releases\"},{\"title\":\"stars/stars/Dicklesworthstone/coding_agent_session_search.md at master · DavidWells/stars\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/DavidWells/stars/blob/master/stars/Dicklesworthstone/coding_agent_session_search.md\"},{\"title\":\"Issues · Dicklesworthstone/coding_agent_session_search\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/Dicklesworthstone/coding_agent_session_search/issues\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here's a comparison of the two tools:\n\n## **Coding Agent Session Search (cass) by Dicklesworthstone**\n\nCoding Agent Session Search is a unified TUI and CLI to index and search local coding agent session history across 11+ providers (Codex, Claude, Gemini, Cursor, Aider, etc.) It uses frankensqlite (a pure-Rust SQLite reimplementation with MVCC multi-writer transactions) as the durable source of truth and frankensearch as a derived speed layer.\n\nKey features include:\n- Auto-discovers sessions from 22 coding agents\n- Pack command for creating compact, cited, extractive artifacts to hand to another agent or human operator\n- Cross-machine search capabilities through SSH/rsync\n\n## **Agent Sessions by jazzyalex**\n\nAgent Sessions is a local-first macOS app to browse, search, analyze, and resume supported AI coding-agent session history across Codex, Claude Code, OpenCode, Cursor Agent, Hermes, OpenClaw, Copilot CLI, and more.\n\nKey features include:\n- Agent Cockpit live command center for active Codex CLI, Claude CLI, and OpenCode CLI iTerm2 sessions, with a compact Quota Meter for usage visibility\n- Right-click Copy Resume Command or Resume for supported CLI sessions, with Terminal.app, iTerm2, and Warp launch targets\n- Local-first with no telemetry, analytics, remote logging, advertising identifiers, or session-history uploads\n\n## **Key Differences**\n\n**Platform**: cass is cross-platform (TUI/CLI), while Agent Sessions is macOS-only (native app).\n\n**Focus**: cass emphasizes unified searching and AI-agent-friendly design; Agent Sessions emphasizes visual browsing, quota tracking, and session resumption.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks