{"actor":{"type":"system"},"content":{"blocks":[{"content":"Web search results for query: \"GitHub Copilot CLI session log local storage hooks 2026\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Using hooks with Copilot CLI for predictable, policy-compliant execution - GitHub Docs\",\"url\":\"https://docs.github.com/en/copilot/tutorials/copilot-cli-hooks\"},{\"title\":\"Using hooks with GitHub Copilot CLI - GitHub Docs\",\"url\":\"https://docs.github.com/en/copilot/how-tos/copilot-cli/customize-copilot/use-hooks\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub Copilot hooks reference - GitHub Docs\",\"url\":\"https://docs.github.com/en/copilot/reference/hooks-reference\"},{\"title\":\"About GitHub Copilot CLI session data - GitHub Docs\",\"url\":\"https://docs.github.com/en/copilot/concepts/agents/copilot-cli/chronicle\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub Copilot CLI Tips & Tricks — Part 4: Automating and enforcing policies with hooks\",\"url\":\"https://bartwullems.blogspot.com/2026/03/github-copilot-cli-tips-tricks-part-4.html\"},{\"title\":\"About hooks for GitHub Copilot - GitHub Docs\",\"url\":\"https://docs.github.com/en/copilot/concepts/agents/hooks\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub Copilot CLI configuration directory - GitHub Docs\",\"url\":\"https://docs.github.com/en/copilot/reference/copilot-cli-reference/cli-config-dir-reference\"},{\"title\":\"Customize agent workflows with hooks - GitHub Docs\",\"url\":\"https://docs.github.com/en/copilot/how-tos/copilot-on-github/customize-copilot/customize-cloud-agent/use-hooks\"},{\"title\":\"copilot-cli/changelog.md at main · github/copilot-cli\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/github/copilot-cli/blob/main/changelog.md\"}]\n\nI've found comprehensive information about GitHub Copilot CLI session logging, local storage, and hooks. Here's what the search results reveal:\n\n## Session Logging and Local Storage\n\nEvery Copilot CLI session is persisted as a set of files in the ~/.copilot/session-state/ directory on your machine. Additionally, Copilot CLI stores structured session data in a local SQLite database, referred to as the session store.\n\nEvery time you use Copilot CLI, your session data is recorded on your local machine. This includes your prompts, Copilot's responses, the tools that were used, and details of files that were modified.\n\n## Hooks for Session Management\n\nHooks are custom scripts that run at specific points during a Copilot CLI session. They can inspect prompts and tool calls, log information for auditing, and even block execution of certain commands.\n\nHooks let you inject your own shell scripts at key moments during a session, enabling everything from audit logging to blocking dangerous commands before they execute.\n\n## Hook Storage Locations\n\nUser-level hook scripts can be stored in ~/.copilot/hooks/. These hooks apply to all your sessions. Repository-level hooks (in .github/hooks/) are loaded alongside user-level hooks.\n\n## Local Storage Practices\n\nA local .github/hooks/logs directory can be used as a simple, illustrative example. These log files are not intended to be committed to the repository and typically live only on a developer's machine.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks.","tool_use_id":"toolu_01RAevm1MRcTqetriqFFnJgV","type":"tool_result"}],"role":"user"},"context":{"branch":"main","cwd":"/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/conversation-ledger","head":"de79e501289e2e19946780867779ef465ead2124","repo":"git@github.com:evintunador/conversation-ledger.git"},"conversation":{"id":"claude-code:700cd82f-2f79-4cd6-b727-0f81230e0837#agent:a4fc099b2ea3fc467","parent":"claude-code:700cd82f-2f79-4cd6-b727-0f81230e0837","seq":70},"id":"ev1-03bc247fbed73fa0d5c6df69622764755acc7a980fe0346f6421ec770b3eb4bf","kind":"conversation_turn","occurred_at":"2026-07-18T23:23:38.355Z","producer":{"session_id":"700cd82f-2f79-4cd6-b727-0f81230e0837","source":"claude-code","source_version":"2.1.214","tool":"cledger","version":"0.20.0"},"raw":{"data":{"agentId":"a4f