:\n\n## Session Storage & Local Data\n\nKimi Code follows a structured data convention with a primary \"Home\" directory (defaulting to ~/.kimi-code/) that stores all persistent state, including configuration, authentication tokens, session history, and logs. This behavior can be overridden via environment variables for specialized environments like CI, remote containers, or portable installations.\n\n## Lifecycle Hooks System\n\nA Hooks System has been implemented inspired by Claude Code, allowing users to configure scripts that trigger at specific lifecycle events (e.g., SessionStart, PreToolUse, UserPromptSubmit), enabling local extensibility without bloating the core tool.\n\nLifecycle hooks can run local commands at key points to gate risky tool calls, audit decisions, trigger desktop notifications, or connect to your own automation.\n\nkimi-mneme, a community plugin, uses all 13 lifecycle events including SessionStart, UserPromptSubmit, PostToolUse, PreCompact, PostCompact, and SessionEnd.\n\n## Hook Configuration\n\nThe hook system is configurable via a user settings file (e.g., ~/.kimi/settings.json or project-local config).\n\nThese features represent Moonshot AI's efforts to make Kimi Code CLI extensible and allow developers to customize lifecycle behavior and session management for their specific workflows.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks.","tool_use_id":"toolu_015cwHfhuS82KTgC1TbV4AT5","type":"tool_result"}],"role":"user"},"context":{"branch":"main","cwd":"/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/conversation-ledger","head":"de79e501289e2e19946780867779ef465ead2124","repo":"git@github.com:evintunador/conversation-ledger.git"},"conversation":{"id":"claude-code:700cd82f-2f79-4cd6-b727-0f81230e0837#agent:a4fc099b2ea3fc467","parent":"claude-code:700cd82f-2f79-4cd6-b727-0f81230e0837","seq":67},"id":"ev1-70266627d1d7b2c68582ef501bd42bfbf497319ba91c29eddcf900e47d9e6d0e","kind":"conversation_tu