{"actor":{"type":"system"},"content":{"blocks":[{"content":"Web search results for query: \"OpenAI Codex CLI 0.144.x hook trust system\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Hooks | ChatGPT Learn\",\"url\":\"https://developers.openai.com/codex/hooks\"},{\"title\":\"Developer commands | ChatGPT Learn\",\"url\":\"https://developers.openai.com/codex/cli/reference\"},{\"title\":\"unable to trust hooks, error in CLI · Issue #22847 · openai/codex\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/openai/codex/issues/22847\"},{\"title\":\"Respect hook trust bypass during TUI startup by etraut-openai · Pull Request #24317 · openai/codex\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/openai/codex/pull/24317\"},{\"title\":\"Agent approvals & security | ChatGPT Learn\",\"url\":\"https://developers.openai.com/codex/agent-approvals-security\"},{\"title\":\"Codex changelog | ChatGPT Learn\",\"url\":\"https://developers.openai.com/codex/changelog\"},{\"title\":\"Provide a supported way for local IDE/wrapper installers to request trust for installed hooks · Issue #21615 · openai/codex\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/openai/codex/issues/21615\"},{\"title\":\"Release 0.144.0 · openai/codex\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/openai/codex/releases/tag/rust-v0.144.0\"},{\"title\":\"OpenAI Codex CLI Cheat Sheet 2026 — 64 Commands | Toolsbase\",\"url\":\"https://toolsbase.dev/en/reference/codex-commands\"},{\"title\":\"Codex Hooks Make the Harness Real\",\"url\":\"https://blakecrosley.com/blog/codex-hooks-make-the-harness-real\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here's what I found about OpenAI Codex CLI's hook trust system in version 0.144.x:\n\n## Hook Trust System Overview\n\nNon-managed command hooks must be reviewed and trusted before they run. Codex requires you to review and trust the exact hook definition, and records trust against the hook's current hash, so new or changed hooks are marked for review and skipped until trusted.\n\n## Managing Hooks\n\nYou can use `/hooks` in the CLI to inspect hook sources, review new or changed hooks, trust hooks, or disable individual non-managed hooks. If hooks need review at startup, Codex prints a warning that tells you to open `/hooks`.\n\n## Hook Sources and Trust Policies\n\nProject-local hooks load only when the project `.codex/` layer is trusted. In untrusted projects, Codex still loads user and system hooks from their own active config layers. Managed hooks from system, MDM, cloud, or requirements.toml sources are marked as managed, trusted by policy, and can't be disabled from the user hook browser.\n\n## Bypassing Hook Trust\n\nFor one-off automation that already vets hook sources outside Codex, you can pass `--dangerously-bypass-hook-trust` to run enabled hooks without requiring persisted hook trust for that invocation.\n\n## Recent Changes in 0.144.x\n\nHook trust bypass now persists through `codex exec` thread start and resume, while blocking PostToolUse hooks correctly reject code-mode tool calls.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks.","tool_use_id":"toolu_017fW9Wo7eRRR5fZdnEu1MrN","type":"tool_result"}],"role":"user"},"context":{"branch":"main","cwd":"/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/conversation-ledger","head":"de79e501289e2e19946780867779ef465ead2124","repo":"git@github.com:evintunador/conversation-ledger.git"},"conversation":{"id":"claude-code:700cd82f-2f79-4cd6-b727-0f81230e0837#agent:a64e77f6bcddcbe2b","parent":"claude-code:700cd82f-2f79-4cd6-b727-0f81230e0837","seq":10},"id":"ev1-4373c6b809c0b2b4576bcec065d4f301361f48de360c4e3be3095a899541fbb9","kind":"conversation_turn","occurred_at":"2026-07-18T22:51:37.487Z","producer":{"session_id":"700cd82f-2f79-4cd6-b727-0f81230e0837","source":"claude-code","source_version":"2.1.214","tool":"cledger","version":"0.20.0"},"raw":{"data":{"agentId":"a64e77f6bcddcbe2b","cwd":"/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/conversation-ledger","entrypoint":"cli","gitBranch":"main","isSidechain":true,"message":{"content":[{"content":"Web search