 after tool execution, at session start/end, and during other key events.\n\n## Hook Types and Functionality\n\nHooks are user-defined scripts or programs that are automatically executed by Qwen Code at predefined points in the application flow. They allow users to execute commands via child processes, with input JSON passed through stdin and output returned via stdout.\n\n## Recent Enhancements (2026)\n\nYou can set up \"auto-trigger\" actions via Hooks. Three new Hook types include HTTP Hooks that send notifications to external services (like Feishu or DingTalk); Function Hooks that execute your own code; and Async Hooks that run long tasks in the background without blocking your current conversation.\n\n## Session Management Features\n\nMemory used to require manual upkeep. Now Qwen Code has auto-memory and auto-dream: the AI extracts important details from your conversations into memory, then periodically reorganizes and prunes it — like tidying a bookshelf — so context flows naturally between sessions.\n\nThe search results show active development of Qwen Code's hook system and session management features throughout 2026, with recent updates focusing on improved notification capabilities and background task execution.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks.","tool_use_id":"toolu_01GpLQnpYPWTj3C7X6rh6hhb","type":"tool_result"}],"role":"user"},"context":{"branch":"main","cwd":"/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/conversation-ledger","head":"de79e501289e2e19946780867779ef465ead2124","repo":"git@github.com:evintunador/conversation-ledger.git"},"conversation":{"id":"claude-code:700cd82f-2f79-4cd6-b727-0f81230e0837#agent:a4fc099b2ea3fc467","parent":"claude-code:700cd82f-2f79-4cd6-b727-0f81230e0837","seq":68},"id":"ev1-f9cb89413f7c7d1edc17b196483946be7c7ff3da2e2e6cfc2dfa1dc9d0655b8b","kind":"conversation_turn","occurred_at":"2026-07-18T23:23:37.896Z","producer":{"session_id":"700cd82f-2f79-4cd6-b727-0f