{"actor":{"type":"system"},"content":{"blocks":[{"content":"Web search results for query: \"\"AI Commit Ledger\" deterministic session attribution git provenance receipt\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"(PDF) AI Commit Ledger: Bridging the AI Transparency Gap in Version Control with Deterministic Session Attribution\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/402524035_AI_Commit_Ledger_Bridging_the_AI_Transparency_Gap_in_Version_Control_with_Deterministic_Session_Attribution\"},{\"title\":\"Agent Provenance: The AI-Debt Radar for AI-Written Code\",\"url\":\"https://www.repowise.dev/guides/agent-provenance\"},{\"title\":\"ai-provenance · GitHub Topics · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/topics/ai-provenance\"},{\"title\":\"The \\\"Provenance-Chain\\\" Standard: Leveraging Git History to Establish 'Original Source' Signals\",\"url\":\"https://blog.trysteakhouse.com/blog/provenance-chain-standard-leveraging-git-history-establish-original-source-signals\"},{\"title\":\"Who Wrote This Code? A Layered Approach to AI Attribution and Provenance\",\"url\":\"https://mattgoodrich.com/posts/ai-code-attribution-and-provenance/\"},{\"title\":\"Provenance as the Chain of Accountability in Agentic Systems\",\"url\":\"https://engineeringagents.substack.com/p/provenance-as-the-chain-of-accountability\"},{\"title\":\"Agent Identity and Signed Provenance: Building Audit Trails for Autonomous Runtime Actions | Zylos Research\",\"url\":\"https://zylos.ai/research/2026-04-25-agent-identity-provenance-signed-audit-trails/\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - git-ai-project/git-ai: A Git extension for tracking the AI-generated code in your repos · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/git-ai-project/git-ai\"},{\"title\":\"Governing Actions, Not Agents: Institutional Attestation as a Governance Model for Autonomous AI Systems\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2606.26298\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here's what I found about AI Commit Ledger and related concepts:\n\n## AI Commit Ledger\n\nAI Commit Ledger is a local-first, Git-native provenance system that generates structured AI Receipts for each commit and persists them in a dedicated metadata branch within the same repository.\n\nThe system was developed in response to the proliferation of AI-assisted development tools such as Claude Code and Cursor Agent, which have transformed software engineering workflows while introducing a gap in commit-level transparency, traceability, and governance.\n\n### Key Features\n\nThe system uses a multi-phase deterministic matching engine that correlates commits with AI agent session artifacts using repository isolation, file overlap scoring, and temporal proximity weighting. The system achieved 94.2% attribution accuracy with sub-400ms overhead per commit.\n\n### The Problem It Addresses\n\nExisting version control systems, including Git, capture the final state of code changes but provide no structured mechanism for recording whether a change was AI-generated, which agent was involved, what prompts or reasoning drove the implementation, or whether governance policies were satisfied.\n\n### Integration\n\nThe system integrates transparently into the standard Git commit lifecycle through repository-scoped post-commit hooks.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks.","tool_use_id":"toolu_01EfZdUpQ5tk5ejRfyA5PS5i","type":"tool_result"}],"role":"user"},"context":{"branch":"main","cwd":"/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/conversation-ledger","head":"de79e501289e2e19946780867779ef465ead2124","repo":"git@github.com:evintunador/conversation-ledger.git"},"conversation":{"id":"claude-code:700cd82f-2f79-4cd6-b727-0f81230e0837#agent:af424cc63295b8016","parent":"claude-code:700cd82f-2f79-4cd6-b727-0f81230e0837","seq":42},"id":"ev1-3c27cbcbf7a75198f09ec39487b771dcf237483931fca3393ff7420cd13ff341","kind":"conversation_turn","occurred_at":"2026-07-18T22:13:57.069Z","producer":{"session_id":"700cd82f-2f79-4cd6-b727-