{"actor":{"type":"system"},"content":{"blocks":[{"content":"Web search results for query: \"\"Codex app\" macOS desktop shares config.toml sessions same as CLI\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"How to Set Up OpenAI Codex (2026): AGENTS.md, MCP Servers, Skills, Config\",\"url\":\"https://llmx.tech/blog/openai-codex-setup-agents-md-mcps-skills-definitive-guide/\"},{\"title\":\"Codex CLI Config Location: ~/.codex Paths (Mac/Linux/Win) | Inventive HQ\",\"url\":\"https://inventivehq.com/knowledge-base/openai/where-configuration-files-are-stored\"},{\"title\":\"Cross-Surface Session Sync: Resuming Codex Sessions Across CLI, Desktop and Cloud | Codex Knowledge Base\",\"url\":\"https://codex.danielvaughan.com/2026/04/08/cross-surface-session-sync/\"},{\"title\":\"[Bug] Codex Mac Desktop app does not load user level config.toml · Issue #25145 · openai/codex\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/openai/codex/issues/25145\"},{\"title\":\"How to Set up MCPs with Codex CLI in 2026 (VS Code, CLI, Codex App) | Composio\",\"url\":\"https://composio.dev/content/how-to-mcp-with-codex\"},{\"title\":\"Advanced Configuration | ChatGPT Learn\",\"url\":\"https://developers.openai.com/codex/config-advanced\"},{\"title\":\"Codex Desktop ignores project .codex/config.toml MCP server (Serena) and only loads ~/.codex/config.toml · Issue #13025 · openai/codex\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/openai/codex/issues/13025\"},{\"title\":\"Developer commands | ChatGPT Learn\",\"url\":\"https://developers.openai.com/codex/cli/reference\"},{\"title\":\"Config basics | ChatGPT Learn\",\"url\":\"https://developers.openai.com/codex/local-config/\"},{\"title\":\"Codex CLI · Hyperskill\",\"url\":\"https://hyperskill.org/learn/step/53566\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I found relevant information about the Codex app and how it handles configuration and sessions across different interfaces.\n\n## Configuration and Sessions Sharing\n\nThe Codex Desktop app shares the same config/skills/MCP setup as other interfaces. However, there are some important nuances:\n\n### Config File Sharing\nSince Codex shares one config.toml across clients, a server you add on the CLI will show up in the app too (the app doesn't have the same detection bug the VS Code extension does). This means the desktop app can access configurations from the global `~/.codex/config.toml`.\n\nHowever, there's a known issue: The Codex desktop app is not loading ~/.codex/config.toml and developer instructions are not being followed, though this works in CLI.\n\nAdditionally, project-scoped .codex/config.toml should be merged into runtime MCP config for trusted projects, but the desktop app doesn't load project-local config while user-global config is loaded.\n\n### Session Sharing\nWith the CLI, Desktop app, IDE extension and Cloud runtime all sharing a unified backend, sessions have become portable artefacts that travel between interfaces. More specifically, a thread started in the CLI can be resumed in the Desktop app without any export/import dance — both connect to the same backend and the same persisted state.\n\nIn summary, while the desktop app is designed to share sessions with the CLI, there are some configuration loading issues that users have reported with the desktop app not properly reading config files.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks.","tool_use_id":"toolu_01DKoofMYBKZf5GFx9fwaThU","type":"tool_result"}],"role":"user"},"context":{"branch":"main","cwd":"/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/conversation-ledger","head":"de79e501289e2e19946780867779ef465ead2124","repo":"git@github.com:evintunador/conversation-ledger.git"},"conversation":{"id":"claude-code:700cd82f-2f79-4cd6-b727-0f81230e0837#agent:a4fc099b2ea3fc467","parent":"claude-code:700cd82f-2f79-4cd6-b727-0f81230e0837","seq":31},"id":"ev1-a853c9c73ddd11d2da3d4f9d6d0107f7f97efc8dd4cfa25fd33767272af50665","kind":"conversation_turn","occurred_at":"2026-07-18T23:22:34.237Z","producer":{