-App Browser for Desktop\nAnthropic released an in-app browser for Claude Code on desktop, allowing the AI coding assistant to interact directly with live versions of webpages. Claude Code's browser appears as a dedicated pane inside the desktop application, and developers can open it with Command-Shift-B on macOS or Control-Shift-B on Windows. Once opened, the browser can sit beside Claude's chat, terminal, file editor, and code-diff views.\n\n### Built-in Browser Features\nClaude Code has a built-in browser that lets the AI open, read, click, and type on web pages directly inside the app. Claude can pull up docs, designs, or any other site. It can read, click through, and interact the same way it does with your local dev servers.\n\n### Chrome Integration\nFor additional browser capabilities, Claude Code can connect to Chrome to test web apps, debug with console logs, automate form filling, and extract data from web pages.\n\n### Web-Based Access\nClaude Code offers quick access from browser, mobile app, or Claude on desktop, great for parallel work or on-the-go coding.\n\nThe platform allows developers to build and test web applications without leaving the Claude Code environment, significantly reducing the need to switch between applications.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks.","tool_use_id":"toolu_019WTsNd2qeRoC2EFnhn9hCc","type":"tool_result"}],"role":"user"},"context":{"branch":"main","cwd":"/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/conversation-ledger","head":"de79e501289e2e19946780867779ef465ead2124","repo":"git@github.com:evintunador/conversation-ledger.git"},"conversation":{"id":"claude-code:700cd82f-2f79-4cd6-b727-0f81230e0837#agent:a4fc099b2ea3fc467","parent":"claude-code:700cd82f-2f79-4cd6-b727-0f81230e0837","seq":49},"id":"ev1-87493dd28278f18f023d5497302d1d318c87af7d99f95cfc574b0b270aa9db80","kind":"conversation_turn","occurred_at":"2026-07-18T23:23:14.342Z","producer":{"session_id":"70