{"actor":{"type":"system"},"content":{"blocks":[{"content":"Web search results for query: \"\"codex\" CLI notify.sh \"agent-turn-complete\" JSON argv last-assistant-message example\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Setup Codex CLI notifications on macOS (iTerm2 + terminal-notifier) | @samwize\",\"url\":\"https://samwize.com/2026/02/05/setup-codex-cli-notifications-on-macos-iterm2-terminal-notifier/\"},{\"title\":\"Codex CLI Guide 2026: Setup, Sandbox, AGENTS.md & MCP\",\"url\":\"https://blakecrosley.com/guides/codex\"},{\"title\":\"Advanced Configuration | ChatGPT Learn\",\"url\":\"https://developers.openai.com/codex/config-advanced\"},{\"title\":\"Advanced Configuration | ChatGPT Learn - OpenAI Developers\",\"url\":\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/docs/config-file/config-advanced\"},{\"title\":\"Codex CLI Agent Notifications: Desktop Alerts, Audio Chimes, and Multi-Agent Monitoring | Codex Knowledge Base\",\"url\":\"https://codex.danielvaughan.com/2026/04/10/codex-cli-agent-notifications-desktop-alerts-monitoring/\"},{\"title\":\"OpenAI Codex CLI Cheat Sheet - Shortcuts and Commands [2026]\",\"url\":\"https://computingforgeeks.com/codex-cli-cheat-sheet/\"},{\"title\":\"Shipyard | Codex CLI Cheatsheet: config, commands, AGENTS.md, + best practices\",\"url\":\"https://shipyard.build/blog/codex-cli-cheat-sheet/\"},{\"title\":\"Codex CLI | ChatGPT Learn\",\"url\":\"https://developers.openai.com/codex/cli\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I found comprehensive information about Codex CLI's notify.sh functionality with the agent-turn-complete event and JSON argv handling.\n\n## Key Findings:\n\nCodex supports a notify hook to run a program when supported events fire — currently only agent-turn-complete.\n\n### Configuration\n\nCodex passes a JSON payload to the command via its arguments. The notify hook is configured in your config file like this:\n\nnotify = [\"/bin/bash\", \"/Users/YOU/.codex/hooks/notify.sh\"]\n\n### JSON Payload Structure\n\nThe notification includes the last-assistant-message field which gives you a preview of what the agent just said. Here's an example from the official documentation:\n\nnotification = json.loads(sys.argv[1]) if notification.get(\"type\") != \"agent-turn-complete\": return 0 title = f\"Codex: {notification.get('last-assistant-message', 'Turn Complete!')}\"\n\n### Bash Example\n\nFor a bash implementation, a minimal notification script for macOS using terminal-notifier extracts the last-assistant-message from the JSON.\n\nThe JSON payload structure includes:\n- `type` - the event type (e.g., \"agent-turn-complete\")\n- `last-assistant-message` - the most recent message from the agent\n- `input-messages` - additional message context\n\nThis allows you to build custom notification systems that react to agent completion events with details about what the agent just accomplished.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks.","tool_use_id":"toolu_01D3R8WsJpV5FT8ycBccToxX","type":"tool_result"}],"role":"user"},"context":{"branch":"main","cwd":"/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/conversation-ledger","head":"de79e501289e2e19946780867779ef465ead2124","repo":"git@github.com:evintunador/conversation-ledger.git"},"conversation":{"id":"claude-code:700cd82f-2f79-4cd6-b727-0f81230e0837#agent:aff74f1a10dad039e","parent":"claude-code:700cd82f-2f79-4cd6-b727-0f81230e0837","seq":64},"id":"ev1-ae9c048fd9811965a80a888d1a14e46d2d465b946dd702a98f141c19ae1a3444","kind":"conversation_turn","occurred_at":"2026-07-18T22:37:41.046Z","producer":{"session_id":"700cd82f-2f79-4cd6-b727-0f81230e0837","source":"claude-code","source_version":"2.1.214","tool":"cledger","version":"0.20.0"},"raw":{"data":{"agentId":"aff74f1a10dad039e","cwd":"/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/conversation-ledger","entrypoint":"cli","gitBranch":"main","isSidechain":true,"message":{"content":[{"content":"Web search results for query: \"\"codex\" CLI notify.sh \"agent-turn-complete\" JSON argv las