{"actor":{"type":"system"},"content":{"blocks":[{"content":"Web search results for query: \"codex exec dangerously-bypass-hook-trust config.toml hooks\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Hooks | ChatGPT Learn\",\"url\":\"https://developers.openai.com/codex/hooks\"},{\"title\":\"prempti/hooks/codex/README.md at main · falcosecurity/prempti\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/falcosecurity/prempti/blob/main/hooks/codex/README.md\"},{\"title\":\"Hooks | ChatGPT Learn - OpenAI Developers\",\"url\":\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/docs/hooks\"},{\"title\":\"Developer commands | ChatGPT Learn\",\"url\":\"https://developers.openai.com/codex/cli/reference\"},{\"title\":\"Project-level .codex/hooks.json is silently ignored when Codex runs inside a git worktree · Issue #27133 · openai/codex\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/openai/codex/issues/27133\"},{\"title\":\"Preserve hook trust bypass in codex exec threads by abhinav-oai · Pull Request #26434 · openai/codex\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/openai/codex/pull/26434\"},{\"title\":\"How to add a Codex hook\",\"url\":\"https://www.simplified.guide/codex/hook-add\"},{\"title\":\"Codex CLI Hooks Reference — hooks.json, PreToolUse & PostToolUse\",\"url\":\"https://agenticcontrolplane.com/blog/codex-cli-hooks-reference\"},{\"title\":\"If you really want stop hooks in Codex, here's something I tried · openai/codex · Discussion #14219\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/openai/codex/discussions/14219\"},{\"title\":\"`--dangerously-bypass-hook-trust` is ignored in TUI mode (codex 0.131.0–0.133.0): \\\"Hooks need review\\\" prompt still blocks startup · Issue #24093 · openai/codex\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/openai/codex/issues/24093\"}]\n\nBased on the web search results, here's what I found about `codex exec --dangerously-bypass-hook-trust` and hooks in config.toml:\n\n## Overview\n\nThe `--dangerously-bypass-hook-trust` flag allows you to run enabled hooks without requiring persisted hook trust for that invocation, intended for one-off automation that already vets hook sources outside Codex.\n\n## Configuration with config.toml and hooks.json\n\nCodex hooks can be configured in two ways:\n\n1. **User-level hooks**: Defined in `~/.codex/hooks.json` and work independently of project state\n2. **Project-level hooks**: Defined in `.codex/hooks.json` at the project root, configured alongside `.codex/config.toml`\n\nCodex accepts inline `[hooks]` tables in config.toml, but keeping hook wiring in hooks.json separates lifecycle commands from general settings.\n\n## Important Considerations\n\n- Do not use `--dangerously-bypass-hook-trust` for normal interactive work; that flag skips persisted hook trust for one invocation and belongs only in automation that vets hook sources separately\n\n- Non-managed command hooks must be reviewed and trusted before they run\n\n- The `codex_hooks` feature flag must be set in `~/.codex/config.toml` — hooks are silently ignored without it\n\nThe flag is particularly useful in CI/CD environments and automation scripts where hook trust has already been verified through external means.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks.","tool_use_id":"toolu_01BZDdGEYeL8ms2173LG8USL","type":"tool_result"}],"role":"user"},"context":{"branch":"main","cwd":"/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/conversation-ledger","head":"de79e501289e2e19946780867779ef465ead2124","repo":"git@github.com:evintunador/conversation-ledger.git"},"conversation":{"id":"claude-code:700cd82f-2f79-4cd6-b727-0f81230e0837#agent:a64e77f6bcddcbe2b","parent":"claude-code:700cd82f-2f79-4cd6-b727-0f81230e0837","seq":9},"id":"ev1-4045752a55613cce4b3f7d326a04e021619421c3cfb5e391b95f3d9712301694","kind":"conversation_turn","occurred_at":"2026-07-18T22:51:35.702Z","producer":{"session_id":"700cd82f-2f79-4cd6-b727-0f81230e0837","source":"claude-code","source_version":"2.1.214","tool":"cledger","version":"0.20.0"},"raw":{"data":{"agentId":"a64e77f6bcddcbe2b","cwd":"/Users/evintunador