enance\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - Dicklesworthstone/pi_agent_rust: High-performance AI coding agent CLI written in Rust with zero unsafe code · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/Dicklesworthstone/pi_agent_rust\"}]\n\nI found several relevant results related to coding agent session history, redaction, append-only logging, and git provenance tools. Here's what the search revealed:\n\n## Key Projects\n\n**ProjectMem** - An event-sourced, plain-text memory substrate for coding agents: an append-only log of typed events (issue / attempt / fix / decision / note) from which a compact, AI-readable summary is deterministically projected. The log is grep-able, diff-able, and git-native—no vector database, no embeddings. It's a local-first, tool-agnostic system with default-on secret redaction.\n\n**Coding Agent Session Search (cass)** - A unified TUI and CLI to search across agent sessions from multiple machines, using SSH/rsync to efficiently sync session data and track provenance. Provenance correlation is project-scoped and explicit-reference anchored, so an unrelated conversation never inherits another's trust.\n\n**Bernstein** - An audit-grade multi-agent orchestration tool with HMAC-chained audit log, signed agent cards, per-artefact lineage, with tamper-evident memory where every cross-session memory write is an append-only, HMAC-tagged chained record.\n\n**Provenance (aybruhm/provenance)** - A compliance middleware with an append-only audit log (hash-chained, tamper-evident) where each entry includes a hash of the previous entry, making tampering detectable.\n\n**Agent AFK** - Features an append-only trace receipt and cross-session memory capabilities.\n\nThese tools collectively address session history management, redaction capabilities, append-only logging for audit trails, and git-based provenance tracking for AI coding agents.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks.","tool_use_id":"toolu_01JDVTmT5