{"actor":{"type":"system"},"content":{"blocks":[{"content":"commit d6705ff7ea32c092c92aefdf69cb6a80e7902a24\nAuthor: Evin Tunador <evintunador@gmail.com>\nDate:   Tue Jul 21 23:36:45 2026 -0700\n\n    Roadmap: cross-account encrypted-reasoning replay verified\n    \n    Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n README.md | 13 +++++++------\n 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 6 deletions(-)\n\ncommit a6126657d66d0f6e0b2b29b05cc7fc6d43f674c2\nAuthor: Evin Tunador <evintunador@gmail.com>\nDate:   Tue Jul 21 23:10:15 2026 -0700\n\n    Roadmap: cross-account reasoning probe needs an account with Codex access\n    \n    Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n README.md | 4 +++-\n 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)\n\ncommit 73d1b35e3ae907030086d92c0a031d1486575180\nAuthor: Evin Tunador <evintunador@gmail.com>\nDate:   Tue Jul 21 17:06:13 2026 -0700\n\n    Roadmap: preserve provider-encrypted reasoning as opaque state\n    \n    Capture drops Codex encrypted_content because we can't read it — but only\n    OpenAI can, they already saw the plaintext, and round-tripping the blob\n    restores hidden reasoning provider-side. Turnbridge probe verified same-\n    account replay acceptance (cross-session, cross-CLI-version). Proposed\n    shape: raw-only opaque tier outside the visible lane, consumer opt-in,\n    provider-matched restore only. Open: cross-account validity, TTL, size.\n    \n    Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n README.md | 20 ++++++++++++++++++++\n 1 file changed, 20 insertions(+)\n---DIFF---\ndiff --git a/README.md b/README.md\nindex fe1f9c0..eaf7aa9 100644\n--- a/README.md\n+++ b/README.md\n@@ -118,7 +118,7 @@ Supported today (built-in, hook-based, per-turn):\n | Source | Trigger | Transcript store | Notes |\n |---|---|---|---|\n | Claude Code CLI | `Stop`/`SessionEnd` hooks | `~/.claude/projects/*/*.jsonl` | Also covers the VS Code extension and JetBrains plugin (both share `~/.claude/set