{"actor":{"type":"system"},"content":{"blocks":[{"text":"Add a \"Security & redaction\" section to /Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/conversation-ledger/README.md. First read the README fully to match its voice and structure (place the new section sensibly — near sync/sharing material if such a section exists), and read docs/WIP_TECHNICAL_DESIGN.md's \"Privacy and integrity\" section, which is the authoritative design. Modify ONLY README.md.\n\nThe section must lay out every security dial, each with (a) what threat it addresses and (b) the cost of changing it. Content to cover:\n\n1. **Threat model in two sentences**: capture-time redaction protects the *shared* record, not the local disk (native CLI transcripts are already plaintext locally); once content is pushed, removal requires coordinated purging — so the layers are ordered prevention-first.\n2. **Capture-time redaction (default on)**: conservative, versioned ruleset of unambiguous token formats (GitHub/Anthropic/OpenAI/AWS/Google/Slack/Stripe/GitLab/npm/SendGrid tokens, PEM private-key blocks, JWTs) replaces matches in both content and raw payload with `[REDACTED:<rule-id>:<fingerprint>]`. Disable via `.cledger.json` `{\"redact\": {\"capture\": false}}` — cost: every future secret lands verbatim.\n3. **Custom patterns**: `{\"redact\": {\"patterns\": [{\"id\": \"my-rule\", \"pattern\": \"...\"}]}}` in `~/.config/cledger/config.json` (global) or `<repo>/.cledger.json` (repo wins).\n4. **Env-value masking (opt-in, default off)**: `{\"redact\": {\"env\": true}}` scrubs exact values of local environment variables and `.env` entries. Cost of enabling: `.env`-as-plain-config values get masked too, and redaction becomes machine-dependent (rescans can produce duplicate events with different ids).\n5. **Sync-time scan (default on)**: before any push of the ledger ref, events the remote doesn't have are scanned with broader rules (keyword assignments like `password=`, URL credentials, bearer tokens); findings block the push. Remediation paths: `cledger redact <event-id>` for real secrets, `cledger allow <fingerprint>` for false positives, `cledger sync --no-scan` to bypass once, config `{\"scan\": {\"tier\": \"off\"}}` to disable permanently (cost: secrets in tool output can be pushed silently). `--paranoid` / `{\"scan\": {\"tier\": \"paranoid\"}}` adds entropy-based detection (noisier).\n6. **`cledger scan [--paranoid]`**: standalone check, exit 1 on findings — CI-friendly.\n7. **`cledger redact <event-id> (--pattern REGEX | --all) [--reason TEXT]`**: rewrites the stored event (placeholder + audit metadata), appends a linked `redaction` event, and — when the ledger has never been pushed — squashes local notes history so the prior content is unrecoverable. After pushing, squash is skipped: shared history retains prior content (post-push purge tooling is planned, not built).\n8. A short \"maximum safety\" recipe: keep all defaults, add repo-specific patterns, enable env masking if your .env holds only secrets, run `cledger scan` in CI, and treat `--no-scan` as a deliberate exception.\n\nKeep it tight — subsection headings or a table for the dials, no marketing fluff, match existing README formatting conventions. Do not commit. Report what you added and where.","type":"text"}],"role":"user"},"context":{"branch":"main","cwd":"/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/conversation-ledger","head":"de79e501289e2e19946780867779ef465ead2124","repo":"git@github.com:evintunador/conversation-ledger.git"},"conversation":{"id":"claude-code:353eecbb-eaf7-4854-a575-a9d56e290707#agent:acceac9e5b51043d7","parent":"claude-code:353eecbb-eaf7-4854-a575-a9d56e290707","seq":0},"id":"ev1-76680b4c5f8bea1c1d504c5bfa5e2c1783aaebab39ee58f10e750610aedbe82d","kind":"conversation_turn","occurred_at":"2026-07-20T03:10:52.714Z","producer":{"session_id":"353eecbb-eaf7-4854-a575-a9d56e290707","source":"claude-code","source_version":"2.1.215","tool":"cledger","version":"0.20.0"},"raw":{"data":{"agentId":"acceac9e5b5