{"actor":{"type":"system"},"content":{"blocks":[{"text":"Build a secret-corpus test harness for the TypeScript project at /Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/conversation-ledger. Another agent is concurrently implementing `src/redact/rules.ts` and `src/redact/apply.ts` to a pinned contract; write against that contract even if the files don't exist yet, and DO NOT create or modify anything under src/redact/ yourself. Style reference: src/test/canonical.test.ts and src/test/helpers.ts (ESM, imports end in `.js`, node:test + node:assert/strict, 2-space indent, zero external runtime deps).\n\nContract you may rely on:\n```ts\nimport { rulesForTier, RULESET_VERSION } from \"../redact/rules.js\";\nimport { redactText } from \"../redact/apply.js\";\n// redactText(text: string, rules) → { text: string; matches: { rule: string; fingerprint: string }[] }\n// rulesForTier(\"capture\") → capture-tier rules only\n```\nCapture-tier rule ids and formats (generate 2–3 format-valid FAKE examples per rule — random-looking but clearly fabricated, never real):\n- github-token: `ghp_`/`gho_`/`ghu_`/`ghs_`/`ghr_` + 36 alphanumerics\n- github-fine-grained: `github_pat_` + 22+ [A-Za-z0-9_]\n- anthropic-api-key: `sk-ant-` + 32+ [A-Za-z0-9_-]\n- openai-api-key: `sk-proj-` + 20+ [A-Za-z0-9_-], and classic `sk-` + exactly 48 alphanumerics\n- aws-access-key-id: `AKIA`/`ASIA` + 16 [A-Z0-9]\n- google-api-key: `AIza` + 35 [0-9A-Za-z_-]\n- slack-token: `xoxb-`/`xoxp-` + 10+ [0-9A-Za-z-]\n- stripe-key: `sk_live_`/`rk_live_` + 24+ alphanumerics\n- gitlab-pat: `glpat-` + 20+ [0-9a-zA-Z_-]\n- npm-token: `npm_` + 36 alphanumerics\n- sendgrid-key: `SG.` + 22 [A-Za-z0-9_-] + `.` + 43 [A-Za-z0-9_-]\n- private-key-block: full `[REDACTED:private-key-block:c2b8191c556b]` (also OPENSSH variant)\n- jwt: `eyJ<10+ b64url>.eyJ<10+ b64url>.<10+ b64url>`\n\nCreate:\n\n1. **src/test/fixtures/secret-corpus.json** — `{ \"positives\": [{ \"rule\": \"<rule-id>\", \"secret\": \"<fake token>\", \"context\": \"<realistic surrounding text, e.g. a fake curl command, .env line, or tool output embedding the secret>\" }...], \"negatives\": [\"<string>\", ...] }`. Negatives must include: a UUID, a 40-hex git SHA, a 64-hex sha256, a base64 image data snippet (~60 chars), an npm package version line, `sk-anthropic` followed by prose, a plain `.env`-style config line with a non-secret value like `THEME=dark-mode-enabled`, a URL without credentials, and a markdown code fence of ordinary code.\n\n2. **src/test/secret-corpus.test.ts** — loads the fixture (JSON.parse + readFileSync with a URL relative to import.meta.url; note tests run compiled from dist/test/, so ALSO copy the fixture via a tsconfig-independent approach: read it from the source tree by resolving `new URL(\"../../src/test/fixtures/secret-corpus.json\", import.meta.url)` — check how dist is laid out: dist/test/*.js means `../../src/test/fixtures/...` resolves correctly from dist/test/). Tests:\n   - every positive: `redactText(context, rulesForTier(\"capture\"))` output does NOT contain `secret`, DOES contain `[REDACTED:`, and at least one match has the expected rule id;\n   - every negative: output is byte-identical to input, zero matches;\n   - determinism: redacting the full concatenated positive corpus twice yields identical output;\n   - a \"gitleaks oracle\" subtest: use node:child_process spawnSync to check `gitleaks version`; if unavailable, `t.skip()`. If available: write the REDACTED outputs of all positive contexts to a temp dir (use fs.mkdtempSync(os.tmpdir())), run `gitleaks detect --no-git --source <dir> --exit-code 1`, assert exit code 0 (no leaks in redacted output). Clean up the temp dir.\n\nVerify your corpus entries actually match the regexes by testing them locally with the regex list above (write a throwaway node script if useful — put it in /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-evintunador-repos-evintunador-conversation-ledger/353eecbb-eaf7-4854-a575-a9d56e290707/scratchpad, not the repo). If `npm test` fails only because src/redact/ doesn't exist yet, that's expected — state it clearly. Do not commit. Do not add dependencies. Report files created and how you validated the corpus.","type":"text"}],"role":"user"},"context":{"branch":"main","cwd":"/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/conversation-ledger","head":"de79e501289e2e19946780867779ef465ead2124","repo":"git@github.com:evintunador/conversation-ledger.git"},"conversation":{"id":"claude-code:353eecbb-eaf7-4854-a575-a9d56e290707#agent:a35b8924ec98376c3","parent":"claude-code:353eecbb-eaf7-4854-a575-a9d56e290707","seq":0},"id":"ev1-3c1a3462139095a752268c7fef6df31cc156c0f3bae611e15aedd05ee2f5637f","kind":"conversation_turn","occurred_at":"2026-07-20T02:57:28.471Z","producer":{"session_id":"353eecbb-eaf7-4854-a575-a9d56e290707","source":"claude-code","source_version":"2.1.215","tool":"cledger","version":"0.20.0"},"raw":{"data":{"agentId":"a35b8924ec98376c3","cwd":"/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/conversation-ledger","entrypoint":"cli","gitBranch":"main","isSidechain":true,"message":{"content":"Build a secret-corpus test harness for the TypeScript project at /Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/conversation-ledger. Another agent is concurrently implementing `src/redact/rules.ts` and `src/redact/apply.ts` to a pinned contract; write against that contract even if the files don't exist yet, and DO NOT create or modify anything under src/redact/ yourself. Style reference: src/test/canonical.test.ts and src/test/helpers.ts (ESM, imports end in `.js`, node:test + node:assert/strict, 2-space indent, zero external runtime deps).\n\nContract you may rely on:\n```ts\nimport { rulesForTier, RULESET_VERSION } from \"../redact/rules.js\";\nimport { redactText } from \"../redact/apply.js\";\n// redactText(text: string, rules) → { text: string; matches: { rule: string; fingerprint: string }[] }\n// rulesForTier(\"capture\") → capture-tier rules only\n```\nCapture-tier rule ids and formats (generate 2–3 format-valid FAKE examples per rule 