{"actor":{"type":"system"},"content":{"blocks":[{"text":"Implement capture-time secret redaction for the TypeScript project at /Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/conversation-ledger. Read docs/WIP_TECHNICAL_DESIGN.md (\"Privacy and integrity\" section) first — it is the authoritative spec. Study src/schema.ts, src/store.ts, src/canonical.ts, and src/test/store.test.ts + src/test/helpers.ts for style (ESM, `.js` import suffixes, node:test + node:assert, 2-space indent, no external deps — keep it that way).\n\nCreate these files EXACTLY to this API contract (other work depends on it):\n\n**src/redact/rules.ts**\n```ts\nexport const RULESET_VERSION = \"cledger-rules/1\";\nexport type RuleTier = \"capture\" | \"standard\" | \"paranoid\";\nexport interface RedactionRule { id: string; tier: RuleTier; description: string; pattern: RegExp; }\nexport const RULES: readonly RedactionRule[];\nexport function rulesForTier(tier: RuleTier): RedactionRule[]; // \"capture\" → capture only; \"standard\" → capture+standard; \"paranoid\" → all\n```\nCapture-tier rules (use these ids and regexes verbatim, all with `g` flag):\n- github-token: `\\b(?:ghp|gho|ghu|ghs|ghr)_[A-Za-z0-9]{36,255}\\b`\n- github-fine-grained: `\\bgithub_pat_[A-Za-z0-9_]{22,255}\\b`\n- anthropic-api-key: `\\bsk-ant-[A-Za-z0-9_-]{32,}\\b`\n- openai-api-key: `\\bsk-(?!ant-)(?:(?:proj|svcacct|admin)-[A-Za-z0-9_-]{20,}|[A-Za-z0-9]{48})\\b`\n- aws-access-key-id: `\\b(?:AKIA|ASIA|ABIA|ACCA)[A-Z0-9]{16}\\b`\n- google-api-key: `\\bAIza[0-9A-Za-z_-]{35}\\b`\n- slack-token: `\\bxox[baprs]-[0-9A-Za-z-]{10,}\\b`\n- stripe-key: `\\b[sr]k_live_[0-9a-zA-Z]{24,}\\b`\n- gitlab-pat: `\\bglpat-[0-9a-zA-Z_-]{20,}\\b`\n- npm-token: `\\bnpm_[A-Za-z0-9]{36}\\b`\n- sendgrid-key: `\\bSG\\.[A-Za-z0-9_-]{22}\\.[A-Za-z0-9_-]{43}\\b`\n- private-key-block: `-----BEGIN (?:RSA |EC |DSA |OPENSSH |PGP )?PRIVATE KEY(?: BLOCK)?-----[\\s\\S]*?-----END (?:RSA |EC |DSA |OPENSSH |PGP )?PRIVATE KEY(?: BLOCK)?-----`\n- jwt: `\\beyJ[A-Za-z0-9_-]{10,}\\.eyJ[A-Za-z0-9_-]{10,}\\.[A-Za-z0-9_-]{10,}\\b`\n\nStandard-tier rules (scan-time; ids: keyword-assignment, url-credentials, bearer-token): keyword-anchored `(?:password|passwd|secret|api_key|apikey|access_token|auth_token|credentials?)[\"']?\\s*[:=]\\s*[\"']?[^\\s\"']{8,}` (case-insensitive), URL creds `[a-z][a-z0-9+.-]*:\\/\\/[^\\s\\/:@]+:[^\\s@]{4,}@` (ci), bearer `\\bbearer\\s+[A-Za-z0-9_\\-.=]{20,}` (ci). Paranoid tier: one rule id `high-entropy` — export also `shannonEntropy(s: string): number` and give the rule a pattern matching candidate tokens `\\b[A-Za-z0-9+/_=-]{24,}\\b`; entropy filtering happens in the scanner later, so just mark the rule; add a boolean field `entropyGated?: true` on that rule.\n\n**src/redact/apply.ts**\n```ts\nexport interface RedactionRecord { rule: string; ruleset: string; fingerprint: string; path: string; }\nexport function redactText(text: string, rules: RedactionRule[]): { text: string; matches: { rule: string; fingerprint: string }[] };\nexport function redactDraft(draft: EventDraft, opts: { rules: RedactionRule[]; extraValues?: string[] }): { draft: EventDraft; records: RedactionRecord[] };\n```\n- Placeholder: `[REDACTED:<rule-id>:<fp>]` where fp = `sha256Hex(matchedText).slice(0, 12)` (use src/canonical.ts's sha256Hex). Deterministic by construction.\n- `redactDraft` deep-walks `draft.content` and `draft.raw.data` (string values only, never object keys), returns a NEW draft (no mutation), records carry a JSON-pointer-ish path like `content/blocks/2/text` or `raw/data/message/content/0/text`.\n- `extraValues`: exact strings (env secrets) to scrub with rule id `env-value` (fingerprint same scheme). Match longest-first to handle overlapping values.\n- Skip entropy-gated rules in redactText (they are scan-only).\n\n**src/redact/config.ts**\n```ts\nexport interface CledgerConfig {\n  redact?: { capture?: boolean; env?: boolean; patterns?: { id?: string; pattern: string }[] };\n  scan?: { tier?: \"standard\" | \"paranoid\" | \"off\" };\n}\nexport async function loadConfig(repoRoot: string): Promise<CledgerConfig>;\nexport function captureRules(config: CledgerConfig): RedactionRule[]; // capture tier + user patterns compiled (invalid regexes skipped silently); [] if redact.capture === false\nexport async function collectEnvValues(repoRoot: string): Promise<string[]>; // only call when redact.env === true\n```\n- loadConfig merges `~/.config/cledger/config.json` then `<repoRoot>/.cledger.json` (repo wins, shallow per-section). Malformed/missing files → ignored silently (capture hooks must never fail a session).\n- collectEnvValues: process.env values with length ≥ 8, excluding names matching common non-secrets (PATH, HOME, PWD, OLDPWD, SHELL, TERM.*, USER, LOGNAME, LANG, LC_.*, EDITOR, VISUAL, PAGER, TMPDIR, DISPLAY, SSH_AUTH_SOCK, XDG_.*), excluding values starting with `/`; plus values parsed from `<repoRoot>/.env` (simple KEY=VALUE lines, quotes stripped, # comments skipped) if it exists.\n\n**src/schema.ts**: add optional `redactions?: RedactionRecord[]` to EvidenceEvent (import the type). It must NOT enter the eventId identity subset. Document why in a comment: rewritten content already determines the id.\n\n**src/store.ts**: in `appendEvents`, before `finalizeEvent`: load config once per call, build capture rules via `captureRules(config)`; if non-empty, gather extraValues when `config.redact?.env === true`, run `redactDraft` on each draft, and attach `redactions` records to the draft when any were produced. Keep the existing behavior byte-identical when nothing matches (existing tests must still pass).\n\n**src/test/redact.test.ts**: node:test suite covering: every capture rule redacts a format-valid fake token and the output contains `[REDACTED:<id>:` and NOT the secret; determinism (same input → identical output twice); placeholders are not re-matched (idempotent on already-redacted text); negatives NOT touched: a UUID, a 40-char git SHA, `sk-anthropic-is-cool`, a normal sentence; deep