{"actor":{"type":"system"},"content":{"blocks":[{"text":"Implement two TypeScript capture adapters for the conversation-ledger project at /Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/conversation-ledger. FIRST read these existing files carefully — your code must compile against them exactly: src/schema.ts, src/store.ts, src/git.ts, src/canonical.ts, src/cli.ts, tsconfig.json (strict, NodeNext ESM — all relative imports need .js extensions; exactOptionalPropertyTypes is ON, so never assign a possibly-undefined value to an optional property, conditionally add the key instead).\n\nCreate exactly two files. Do not modify any existing file. Zero runtime dependencies (node stdlib only).\n\n=== File 1: src/adapters/claude-code.ts ===\nExports:\n- `export async function runClaudeCodeHook(stdinJson: string): Promise<void>` — parses the Claude Code hook payload JSON: fields include session_id, transcript_path, cwd, hook_event_name. Behavior: if cwd is not inside a git repo (use findRepo from ../git.js), exit silently (return, exit code 0 — hooks must never break the user's session; wrap everything so ANY error prints one line to stderr and returns without throwing). Otherwise call captureClaudeTranscript(transcript_path, cwd).\n- `export async function captureClaudeTranscript(transcriptPath: string, cwd: string): Promise<void>` — reads the transcript JSONL file, converts lines to EventDraft[], calls appendEvents(repo, drafts) from ../store.js. Print a one-line summary to stderr like `cledger: claude-code +N events (M deduped)`.\n\nTranscript format (~/.claude/projects/<escaped-cwd>/<session-id>.jsonl), one JSON object per line. Only convert lines where type is \"user\" or \"assistant\" AND isSidechain is not true AND the line has a `message` field. Skip types: system, summary, ai-title, last-prompt, mode, permission-mode, attachment, file-history-snapshot, file-history-delta, queue-operation, and anything unrecognized. Envelope fields per line: uuid, parentUuid, sessionId, timestamp (ISO8601), cwd, gitBranch, version.\n\nMapping each kept line (line index in the FILE = seq, counting ALL lines including skipped ones, 0-based — must be stable across re-scans):\n- kind: \"conversation_turn\"\n- occurred_at: line.timestamp\n- actor: user lines → { type: \"human\" }; assistant lines → { type: \"agent\", id: message.model } (add id only if model present)\n- producer: { tool: \"cledger\", version: <package version — read ../../package.json via new URL relative import at runtime like cli.ts does, or hardcode \"0.1.0\">, source: \"claude-code\", session_id: line.sessionId }\n- conversation: { id: \"claude-code:\" + line.sessionId, seq }\n- content: { role: message.role, blocks: [...] } where blocks normalize message.content: if content is a string → [{type:\"text\", text}]; if array → map each block: {type:\"text\",text} kept as-is; {type:\"tool_use\",id,name,input} kept; {type:\"tool_result\",tool_use_id,content} kept (content may be string or array — keep verbatim); {type:\"thinking\",thinking} → {type:\"thinking\", text: thinking} but OMIT the signature field; unknown block types kept verbatim.\n- raw: { format: \"claude-code-jsonl/1\", data: <the original parsed line object> }\n- Do NOT set context (appendEvents fills it) or id/recorded_at.\n\nCursor optimization (correctness does not depend on it — appendEvents dedups by id): store per-session cursor at <repo.gitDir>/conversation-ledger/cursors/<sessionId>.json with {lines: <number of file lines already processed>}. On capture: read cursor; if the file now has fewer lines than the cursor, reset cursor to 0; convert only lines at index >= cursor; after a successful append, write the new cursor (total line count). Use sessionId sanitized to [A-Za-z0-9_-] for the filename. Create dirs with mkdir recursive.\n\n=== File 2: src/adapters/codex.ts ===\nExports:\n- `export async function runCodexHook(stdinJson: string): Promise<void>` — Codex CLI hooks-engine payload: session_id, transcript_path, cwd, hook_